    ('65d8b64d-00d7-5269-93d5-be73f809cf84', 'a414061f-cd1c-5819-93ce-6c073903cea1', 'Shopify Website Builder for Electronics Store', 'I need help building a Shopify website for my electronics business. The project includes setting up the store, creating product pages, organizing categories, and improving the overall shopping experience. I’m looking for someone who can work efficiently, communicate clearly, and deliver a clean, functional site that supports my business goals.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('decc12b7-45a2-5984-84fb-22a8fdf93745', 'ff07551a-a3b2-5319-adf2-37b95a859dff', 'Shopify Website Builder for Clothing Store', 'I need help building a Shopify website for my clothing store. The project includes setting up the store, creating product pages, organizing collections, and improving the overall shopping experience. I’m looking for someone who can work efficiently, communicate clearly, and deliver a polished storefront that looks professional and functions smoothly.', 1, 'HOURLY', 310000.00, 697000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('bb096d7c-d04c-5c12-9e37-38261e553b90', '68bb4561-3505-501f-97e8-eab81d844f05', 'Shopify Specialist for Team Sports Apparel Store', 'I need a Shopify specialist to help launch a team sports apparel store quickly using my existing Shopify setup. The work includes creating and uploading artwork for jerseys, hoodies, T-shirts, hats, and other merchandise, setting up pricing based on costs and target selling prices, and configuring sizes and variants for youth and adult products. You should also organize the store so parents and players can easily find their team’s gear. This is not a rebuild project, so I need someone who can work within the current setup, move fast, and communicate clearly throughout the process.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 646000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('70217e1a-2b91-5408-86d2-ab9c1e41a05a', 'cb19167f-8993-5377-9264-f6f503a77dcb', 'Shopify Website Builder for Furniture Business', 'I need help building a Shopify website for my office furniture business. The site should be clean, professional, and easy to navigate, with clear product pages and a smooth checkout experience. I’m looking for someone who can create a polished storefront, organize product listings, and ensure the site is ready for launch. Please share examples of similar Shopify projects and your approach to building a reliable online store.', 1, 'HOURLY', 310000.00, 697000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('3c733aad-9a94-5ba8-bdc8-f2a733716bf6', 'cb19167f-8993-5377-9264-f6f503a77dcb', 'Shopify Website Developer for Furniture Store', 'I am looking for a skilled Shopify developer to build a professional online store for my office furniture business. The website should have a modern, attractive design, clear product listings with high-quality images and pricing, a shopping cart, secure payment options, mobile-friendly layout, product categories, search functionality, easy inventory management, and SEO support. I also need a contact page and WhatsApp integration for customer inquiries. Please share examples of similar Shopify stores you have built, your estimated cost, and the timeline for completing the project.', 1, 'HOURLY', 310000.00, 697000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0b5cf7e2-5dc9-502f-b85f-59564b020a2b', 'ee3a4ba8-53f0-5611-aca2-22404d13fe5b', 'Shopify Landing Page designer needed', 'We need a designer to create a polished landing page for our Shopify store. The page should be visually appealing, easy to navigate, and optimized for conversions. You will work with our team to understand the brand, audience, and goals, then deliver a clean, responsive design that supports our marketing efforts. Experience creating high-converting Shopify pages is important, and we’re looking for someone who can turn ideas into a strong user experience.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('2a155376-2efe-5558-a7da-bbf96731789e', 'ee3a4ba8-53f0-5611-aca2-22404d13fe5b', 'Shopify Store Development with Sproket', 'We need a developer to build a beautiful Shopify store for US dropshipping using Sproket. The project includes setting up the store, customizing the theme, improving the overall look and feel, and ensuring the site is clean, modern, and easy to navigate. Experience with Shopify and Sproket is important, along with the ability to create a polished storefront that supports a strong customer experience.', 1, 'FIXED', 2196000.00, 2196000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('de2dd3c0-2dcc-563f-a994-cd90b88afa7b', '0eb58ffa-9612-5cb9-bdf9-23a824ab61eb', 'DTC Product Researcher & Shopify Product Page Specialist', 'We are a seven-figure DTC ecommerce company looking for an experienced specialist who can: 1. Find products with verified customer demand. 2. Identify underserved customer segments. 3. Build premium, conversion-focused Shopify product pages. This is not an entry-level product-hunting or general VA role. We do not want random TikTok products, copied competitor research, or AI-generated assumptions. Your Responsibilities: - Research problem-solving, evergreen, or strongly giftable products for the US market. - Validate demand through Google Trends, competitors, customer reviews, Reddit, TikTok comments, and relevant Facebook discussions. - Identify two underserved customer avatars for each shortlisted product. - Identify five distinct customer desires or reasons to buy. - Estimate TAM, supported by credible sources and clear assumptions. - Analyze Amazon one- and two-star reviews to find product weaknesses and improvement opportunities. - Evaluate competition, saturation, positioning, pricing, offers, and estimated economics. - Recommend TEST, RESEARCH FURTHER, or REJECT. - After approval, create premium Shopify product pages using research-driven copy, offers, and AI-assisted product imagery. Weekly Deliverables Provide 3–5 thoroughly researched product opportunities each week. Each opportunity must include: - Customer problem and product solution - Two underserved avatars - Five customer desires - Manual Reddit, Facebook, and TikTok findings - Amazon negative-review analysis - Google Trends chart - TAM estimate and methodology - Competitor and saturation analysis - Product-improvement recommendations - Potential offer and positioning - Risks and final recommendation - Source links and research dates Approved products must then be developed into test-ready Shopify product pages. What We Need - Proven DTC product-research experience - Strong customer psychology and commercial judgment - Shopify product-page creation experience - Conversion-focused ecommerce copywriting - Competence with modern AI image and research tools - Ability to create professional product imagery—not cheap-looking AI graphics - Understanding of product costs, margins, offers, refunds, and fulfillment risks - Excellent written English - Fast, independent execution with same-day communication about blockers AI may assist your work, but it must not replace manual research or source verification. Immediate Deadline You must be available to begin immediately. Do not apply if you cannot work quickly while maintaining research quality. Do Not Apply If You - Call products “guaranteed winners” - Rely only on TikTok trends or product-spy tools - Treat active competitor advertisements as proof of profitability - Submit generic AI-generated research - Cannot provide supporting links - Copy competitors’ pages, images, or advertisements - Create broad avatars such as “women aged 25–55” - Need constant supervision or several days to provide progress How to Apply Please include: 1. An example of a product-research report you personally completed. 2. Links or screenshots of Shopify product pages you created. 3. Examples of AI-assisted product imagery you produced. 4. A product you previously rejected and the commercial reason for rejecting it. 5. The research, Shopify, and AI tools you use. 6. Confirmation that you can begin immediately and meet the Thursday deadline. Applications without relevant work samples will not be considered. Screening Questions 1. How do you determine whether demand is genuine rather than temporary hype? 2. How would you identify an underserved avatar for a product that already has competitors? 3. What information must accompany a Google Trends chart? 4. How do you estimate TAM without confusing the number of people with a problem with the number likely to purchase? 5. Describe how you turn Reddit comments and negative Amazon reviews into product-page messaging and product improvements. 6. Which parts of your research must be completed manually rather than by AI? 7. How do you decide whether to test or reject a product? Shortlisted applicants will complete a brief practical assessment involving demand evidence, customer research, commercial judgment, and a product-page concept.', 1, 'HOURLY', 310000.00, 646000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4aa1b5da-db0c-51a2-af96-6a4fb48847fc', '05d93356-6a89-5a59-b303-b684dd46887d', 'Shopify CRO Expert & Developer — Ongoing Role for Established U.S. E-Commerce Store', '# Senior Shopify CRO Expert & Developer — Ongoing Role for Established U.S. E-Commerce Store (Individuals Only) **Job Type:** Ongoing / Long-Term Freelance **Experience Level:** Expert **Engagement:** Part-time, with potential for increased hours **Website:** https://www.databazaar.com **Platform:** Shopify **Applicants:** Individual freelancers only — NO agencies ## About Us Databazaar.com is an established U.S.-based e-commerce retailer with a long operating history, selling fine jewelry, lab-grown and natural diamonds, certified gemstones, designer fragrances, fine leather goods, and gifts. We are looking for an exceptional **Shopify developer who is also a proven Conversion Rate Optimization (CRO) specialist** to take ownership of our store''s technical performance, user experience, and conversion improvements. Our store already receives traffic, but we are experiencing significant drop-offs throughout the shopping funnel, particularly between product discovery, add-to-cart, checkout, and completed purchases. **We do not need someone who simply maintains a Shopify website. We need someone who knows how to turn visitors into paying customers.** This is intended to become a long-term working relationship with an individual freelancer who can independently identify problems, recommend solutions, implement improvements, and demonstrate measurable results. ## 1. Conversion Rate Optimization — Your Primary Responsibility - Conduct a comprehensive CRO audit of our Shopify storefront, including homepage, collection pages, product pages, cart, and checkout. - Analyze the entire customer journey to identify friction points, abandonment causes, and lost conversion opportunities. - Diagnose why visitors add products to their carts but fail to proceed to checkout or complete purchases. - Identify and address mobile conversion problems, particularly on smartphones. - Evaluate product-page layouts, purchase buttons, trust elements, product descriptions, delivery information, and overall usability. - Improve cart design and cart-to-checkout progression. - Investigate checkout abandonment, payment issues, unexpected shipping charges, and customer hesitation. - Implement effective cart-abandonment and exit-intent solutions, including checkout-stage solutions where technically supported by Shopify. - Design and execute structured A/B tests using appropriate Shopify-compatible tools. - Recommend and implement high-impact changes based on actual customer behavior and data, not assumptions. - Optimize conversion separately for different product categories, recognizing that expensive jewelry and designer fragrances have different purchase considerations. - Continuously monitor conversion performance and proactively recommend improvements. **Your success will be measured primarily by improvements in completed purchases, conversion rate, and revenue per visitor—not by how many development tasks you complete.** ## 2. Shopify Development & Ongoing Maintenance You must also be an accomplished, hands-on Shopify developer capable of handling our regular technical requirements. Responsibilities include: - Shopify Liquid, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and theme development. - Maintain, troubleshoot, and optimize our existing Shopify theme. - Implement minor design changes, layout improvements, and new website features. - Fix bugs, broken functionality, and technical issues promptly. - Maintain product-page templates, collection layouts, navigation, filters, and search functionality. - Troubleshoot Shopify apps, integrations, and third-party scripts. - Optimize mobile responsiveness and cross-browser compatibility. - Improve page-loading speed and Core Web Vitals. - Identify unnecessary apps, conflicting scripts, and performance bottlenecks. - Maintain checkout-related functionality within Shopify''s platform and plan limitations. - Ensure website updates do not disrupt existing functionality, product feeds, or integrations. - Implement changes using appropriate testing, backups, version control, and rollback procedures. - Handle small, routine maintenance requests efficiently without requiring constant supervision. Our day-to-day maintenance workload is relatively modest. We are looking for someone who can combine these responsibilities with continuous CRO improvement. ## 3. Analytics, Tracking & Technical Diagnosis Strong analytics expertise is essential. - Advanced working knowledge of Google Analytics 4 (GA4), Google Tag Manager, Shopify Analytics, and Google Search Console. - Audit and correct tracking for product views, add-to-cart, checkout initiation, payment steps, and completed purchases. - Identify duplicate, missing, or incorrectly triggered analytics events. - Reconcile GA4 conversion reporting with actual Shopify orders. - Investigate abnormal traffic spikes, suspicious traffic, and possible bot activity. - Analyze conversion by device, traffic source, landing page, and product category. - Implement or manage heatmaps, session recordings, and behavior analytics tools such as Microsoft Clarity or Hotjar. - Identify technical issues affecting Google Shopping, Meta Pixel, and other marketing integrations. - Create clear, actionable conversion dashboards and performance reports. We currently have evidence of significant discrepancies between analytics events and actual completed purchases. The successful candidate must be comfortable investigating complex tracking and attribution problems. ## 4. Trust, Credibility & Purchase Confidence We want to make Databazaar a store where customers feel completely confident making purchases, including high-value purchases. - Improve presentation of authentic customer reviews and independently verifiable trust credentials. - Optimize product authenticity messaging, particularly for designer fragrances, jewelry, and luxury goods. - Improve shipping and delivery estimates and ensure consistent information across the website. - Clearly communicate returns, refunds, and customer support policies. - Eliminate contradictory delivery promises and confusing countdown timers. - Improve reassurance around secure payments and order fulfillment. - Evaluate and implement trust-building elements that genuinely improve conversions. - Avoid misleading badges, fabricated urgency, false scarcity, or other deceptive CRO techniques. ## 5. Proactive Store Optimization We do not want a freelancer who simply waits for instructions. We expect you to: - Regularly review store performance and identify opportunities. - Maintain a prioritized CRO improvement backlog. - Recommend improvements based on potential commercial impact. - Implement approved improvements independently. - Monitor results and adjust unsuccessful changes. - Communicate directly with our digital marketing manager when needed. - Provide concise weekly updates covering completed changes, findings, and measured outcomes. - Take responsibility for technical quality, conversion performance, and the overall shopping experience. ## 6. Required Qualifications **Please apply only if you meet ALL of the following:** - Minimum 5 years of professional Shopify development experience. - At least 3 years of hands-on e-commerce CRO experience. - Demonstrated experience improving conversion rates for established Shopify stores. - Expert knowledge of Shopify Liquid, JavaScript, CSS, theme architecture, and Shopify APIs. - Strong practical knowledge of Shopify checkout capabilities and limitations. - Proven ability to diagnose checkout abandonment and conversion funnel problems. - Advanced GA4, Google Tag Manager, and Shopify Analytics skills. - Experience with A/B testing and customer behavior analytics. - Strong mobile UX and performance optimization skills. - Ability to work independently and communicate clearly in English. - Willingness to personally perform the development work rather than subcontract it. Experience with luxury goods, jewelry, fragrances, fashion accessories, or other high-consideration e-commerce categories is a significant advantage. **Shopify Partner or Shopify Expert credentials are desirable, but proven CRO results matter much more than certifications.** ## 7. Initial 30-Day Assignment The first month will be a paid evaluation period. **Week 1 — Audit & Diagnosis** - Analyze Shopify and GA4 conversion data. - Audit the mobile and desktop customer journey. - Identify the top 10 conversion barriers. - Review tracking accuracy and checkout functionality. - Deliver a prioritized action plan with estimated implementation effort. **Week 2 — High-Impact Fixes** - Implement approved high-priority fixes. - Address critical usability and trust problems. - Correct identified technical errors. - Establish reliable conversion measurement. **Week 3 — CRO Improvements** - Improve selected product pages and cart experience. - Implement approved conversion experiments. - Optimize mobile shopping flows. - Test trust and purchase-confidence improvements. **Week 4 — Measurement & Roadmap** - Evaluate results against the established baseline. - Report improvements in conversion and revenue per visitor. - Identify which changes worked and which did not. - Present a prioritized 60-day CRO roadmap. We understand that meaningful CRO results require sufficient traffic, clean measurement, and appropriate testing periods. We expect rigorous analysis, not unrealistic guarantees. ## 8. Long-Term Engagement Following a successful initial month, we envision an ongoing part-time relationship involving: - Routine Shopify development and maintenance. - Continuous conversion analysis and optimization. - Regular improvements to the shopping experience. - Troubleshooting and technical monitoring. - Monthly CRO priorities and performance reporting. - Collaboration with our in-house digital marketing manager. We prefer an experienced individual who can provide consistent support over the long term rather than a rotating team of developers. ## 9. How to Apply — Mandatory Screening Questions **Generic proposals and AI-generated cover letters without specific evidence of relevant experience will not be considered.** Please answer ALL the following questions: 1. **CRO Results:** Provide two examples of Shopify stores where you personally improved conversion rates. Include the original conversion rate, resulting conversion rate, time period, changes implemented, and how results were measured. 2. **Checkout Diagnosis:** A Shopify store receives substantial traffic and add-to-cart activity, but very few completed purchases. What are the first five things you would investigate, and in what order? 3. **Analytics Expertise:** GA4 reports thousands of `begin_checkout` events but very few purchases, while Shopify reports substantially different checkout numbers. How would you determine whether the problem is actual abandonment or faulty tracking? 4. **Technical Skills:** Describe a technically challenging Shopify issue you personally diagnosed and fixed. Explain the root cause and your implementation. 5. **CRO Tools:** Which tools do you personally use for heatmaps, session recordings, A/B testing, performance analysis, and funnel optimization? Why? 6. **Availability & Pricing:** How many hours per week can you commit? What is your hourly rate, and what would you estimate for the initial 30-day audit and optimization engagement? 7. **Individual Confirmation:** Confirm that you are an independent freelancer, that you will personally perform the work, and that you will not subcontract it. 8. **Databazaar Assessment:** Spend 10–15 minutes reviewing https://www.databazaar.com and identify three specific opportunities for improving conversions. Explain why you selected them. No purchase is required. ## Important We are looking for an **analytical CRO specialist who can code**, not a developer who merely knows how to install conversion apps. If you have successfully transformed underperforming Shopify stores into higher-converting businesses, can demonstrate your results, and enjoy taking ownership of a long-term e-commerce project, we would like to hear from you. **Individual freelancers only. No agencies, development companies, or outsourced teams.**', 1, 'HOURLY', 207000.00, 646000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b5a50542-b6b8-565d-919f-4392b7e91a26', '9e288041-7718-598f-b153-1bfd6e149d0e', 'Need an n8n automation expert to take over our Shopify order admin', 'I run a Shopify store selling home goods, around 300 to 400 orders a month. Behind the scenes it’s a mess of spreadsheets, copied and pasted order details, and a morning routine that eats up time. Between the two of us it adds up to about 15 hours a week, and I’d like to get that time back. I’m looking for someone who has built this kind of thing before and can explain it to me without jargon. This is what I need: New Shopify orders go into our Google Sheet automatically, get labelled by shipping region, and the right details are emailed to our fulfillment partner. Today I do this by hand every morning. Suspicious orders get caught early. Think mismatched billing and shipping addresses, large first orders from new customers, or someone requesting refunds again and again. These should land in Slack so we can check them before they ship. Customers get a shipping notification, then a follow up a week after delivery asking for a review. If someone replies with a complaint, we get alerted instead of it sitting unseen in an inbox. Every Monday morning, a short email with the week’s sales, refunds and best selling products. We already have Shopify, Google Workspace and Slack set up. I lean towards n8n, either cloud or self hosted (I’d like your opinion on which suits us), because I don’t want pricing that climbs with every task we run. If you think another tool is a better fit, say so and tell me why. Reliability matters most to me. I’ve had automations quietly stop working before and didn’t notice for days. So I expect proper error handling, retries and some kind of alert or log when something fails. When you finish, I need a short video or written guide so I can understand how it works and fix small things myself. It’s a plus if you’ve used AI to sort support emails or draft replies, as that may be our next phase. What to include in your proposal Please skip the standard introduction. I’d rather read about one similar automation you actually built: what it did, the tools involved, what broke during the project and how you solved it. A screenshot or short screen recording would help a lot. Also give me a few sentences on how you’d handle point 2, the order flagging, since that’s the part I’m least sure how to set up. Timing and budget I’m flexible on budget for the right person and would rather pay fairly for tidy, documented work than go with the cheapest bid. I’d like to begin this week and wrap up within 3 to 4 weeks, with ongoing monthly support possible if things go well.', 1, 'FIXED', 15499000.00, 15499000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4231be95-7ac5-52f6-bd11-29f5e43671bf', '9e288041-7718-598f-b153-1bfd6e149d0e', 'Shopify + GoHighLevel Integration & Follow-Up Automation Expert', 'We are looking for an expert to help organise, manage and improve our existing, functioning Shopify store, Eden Valley Market. This is not a build-from-scratch job. We would like the store polished and improved so it is secure and beautifully built, Shopify connected and integrated with GoHighLevel (and any other tools needed for this work), and marketing started right away. The work includes follow-up automation, including cart abandonment and retargeting, and other related marketing efforts. Please share examples of similar work you have completed successfully. This is a $50 fixed-price starting engagement, with the scope above as the first step.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('96c456b2-f6d0-52ed-9b6b-30cda8d4e5da', 'e441bbf0-43d8-5964-8784-4308b18f9940', 'Create Shopify Store', 'I need help creating a Shopify store for my business. The work includes setting up the store, adding products, and making sure everything is ready for customers to shop. I’m looking for someone who can complete the setup quickly and clearly explain what was done. Please share examples of similar Shopify stores you’ve built and your availability for this project.', 1, 'FIXED', 129000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('9feaf226-c4e8-5251-bb1e-c69cdd7a5a39', '530de989-596f-537f-b28b-e5f4b5037c8d', 'Senior Next.js / TypeScript developer: help scale a Shopify checkout platform', 'We run Revio, a hosted, branded checkout for Shopify stores. Merchants add one script to their store. Their shoppers then check out on our faster, customisable page, with a drag-and-drop builder, order bumps, post-purchase offers, A/B tests, Google Pay/Apple Pay and ad-platform tracking. It is live and processing real orders. We are a small team, and I am looking for a strong developer to work with me on the next stage. Our stack Next.js 16 (App Router, server components), React, TypeScript, Tailwind Prisma 7 on Neon Postgres, deployed on Vercel Shopify Admin and Storefront GraphQL APIs, plus a storefront embed script Whop Elements for payments (card, Google Pay, Apple Pay, local methods), and webhooks Google Ads, Meta CAPI and TikTok tracking, server-side Playwright and Vitest for testing What you would work on (first 3 months) Checkout speed and conversion. Benchmark against the best checkouts in the market, and cut time to a usable page and to payment-ready. We already have a lab benchmark harness. We need someone who enjoys shaving 100 ms off real devices. Experimentation. A proper old-versus-new test framework with sticky cookies, per-variant reporting and stop rules, so we can prove what raises conversion instead of guessing. Tracking you can trust. Server-side conversion events (Google, Meta, TikTok), deduplication, funnel analytics (“opened, filled, paid”) and clean session and bot filtering. Payments and edge cases. Wallet buttons across Safari, in-app browsers (Instagram, Facebook, Google app) and Android. Discount stacking with Shopify’s combination rules. Multi-currency. Free and zero-total orders. Subscriptions. Reliability. Monitoring, alerts, safer rollouts (feature flags, kill switches) and test coverage on the money paths. Product features. Post-purchase offers, order-bump and upsell logic, new checkout blocks, and a merchant dashboard. You are a good fit if you Have 5+ years of professional TypeScript and React, and have shipped production Next.js (App Router) apps Are comfortable with Postgres and Prisma (or a similar ORM), including safe migrations on a live database Have built or integrated payment flows (Stripe, Adyen, Whop or similar) and understand webhooks, idempotency and failure modes Have worked with the Shopify APIs (Admin or Storefront GraphQL), or can learn them fast Care about web performance (Core Web Vitals, hydration, bundle size, caching) Test your work in a real browser, including Safari and mobile, and report honestly what you did and did not verify Communicate clearly in English and work independently Nice to have Experience with conversion rate optimisation or A/B testing infrastructure Ads tracking (Google gtag and enhanced conversions, Meta Conversions API, TikTok Events API) Vercel, edge and caching knowledge, and Playwright or visual regression testing Experience in e-commerce or a checkout, cart or payments product How we work Async-first, with short written updates. We use Git and small, reviewed pull requests. Production changes go out in small steps, with a way to roll back quickly. Contract, 15 to 25 hours a week to start, with room to grow. Time zone overlap of 3+ hours with the Netherlands (CET) is a plus. Rate: [your range]. We start with a small paid test task (about 1 to 2 days), then a longer engagement if it goes well. To apply, please answer: Describe a payment or checkout flow you built or fixed. What went wrong in production, and how did you find it? How would you measure and improve the load time of a server-rendered checkout page on a mid-range phone? How would you set up an A/B test on a low-traffic site, and how do you decide when to stop it? Link to your best work, such as a repo, product or write-up. And come up with improvements for our platform (www.revio-checkout.com)', 1, 'HOURLY', 129000.00, 387000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('74fd9cab-3c6b-5ad4-af8e-9e7e3823d1f6', 'e2e4e63d-1b3b-502c-b4d3-327b0346e0e6', 'Shopify Developer Needed to Improve Store Design and Increase Conversions', 'I''m looking for an experienced Shopify developer to help improve my existing online store. The website is already live, but I''m not satisfied with the overall design, especially on mobile. Some product pages need improvement, the navigation could be easier to use, and I feel the current layout isn''t doing enough to encourage customers to buy. I need someone who can review the store, identify what''s holding it back, and make practical improvements. The work will include: Improving the homepage and product page layouts. Making the website more responsive on mobile. Improving navigation and collection pages. Optimizing website speed and overall performance. Making the shopping and checkout experience smoother. Suggesting improvements that could help increase conversions. I''m not looking for someone who will simply install a new theme. I want a Shopify expert who understands both website design and how customers shop online. Please share examples of Shopify stores you''ve worked on, explain how you''d approach this project, and let me know your estimated timeline.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('6794dc3e-3b0f-591e-acad-2e1c224df8ea', 'e2e4e63d-1b3b-502c-b4d3-327b0346e0e6', 'Need a Shopify Developer to Fix Some Issues on My Store', 'I need a Shopify developer to help fix issues on my store. The work includes reviewing the current setup, identifying problems, and making the necessary updates to improve functionality and performance. I’m looking for someone who can communicate clearly, work efficiently, and deliver reliable fixes. If you have experience troubleshooting Shopify stores and improving site performance, I’d love to hear how you would approach this project.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('02bdd708-3cd5-5572-83c2-4b3fad4e2dda', '5cfef850-3286-5bc8-b6e9-66f0dc1c8a70', 'Shopify Website for Pet Care Store', 'I need help creating a Shopify website for my pet care store. The project includes setting up the store, organizing products, and making the site easy to use for customers. I’m looking for someone who can build a clean, functional online store and help me launch it smoothly. Please share examples of similar Shopify projects and your experience with e-commerce websites.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('74166cf7-5f2b-507c-8483-9b5337fa3c4b', 'ff354a04-0484-58b9-ab32-d29ff1c61eb9', 'Ecommerce Automation N8N Shopify Zoho Klaviyo Claude', 'We''re an online supplier of commercial kitchen equipment. We sell across Shopify (AU + NZ), eBay, Kogan, Bunnings, Harvey Norman, TradeMe and Google Shopping. We run our business on Google sheets, Claude and n8n. We also have custom backend dashboard in Laravel which handles many of our operations. This job is about automating many old legacy tasks we are still doing manually. Depending how that goes and how quick you learn our systems, this could turn into a full time role. Your first 90 days Automate our recurring ecommerce tasks. We have more than 50 daily, weekly and monthly jobs that are done by hand today: supplier price and stock imports, promotion setup, datafeed checks, marketplace and Google Merchant Center errors, sold and discontinued product cleanup. Your job is to make them run without a person, verify them, then shut down the manual process. After that, you''ll have the option to grow into the full Ecommerce Manager role. You must know Claude: - Claude Projects, skills and scheduled tasks - Connecting Claude to business apps through connectors / MCP (Shopify, Zoho, Google Sheets, Gmail, Klaviyo) - When to use Claude, when to use n8n, and when to use a simple script - Writing clear instructions so Claude gets it right the first time Must have - Built real automations in n8n (show us examples) - 2+ years working in Shopify, ideally multi-channel or marketplace sellers - Comfortable with Google Sheets, CSVs, APIs and webhooks - You check your own work. Done means verified live on the site or marketplace, not "I clicked save". Bonus points - Python or JavaScript - Omnivore, Google Merchant Center, Shopify Admin API / GraphQL - Zoho CRM / Projects - Large catalogues (10,000+ SKUs) How we work - Every task has a "Done when" outcome that can be checked - You update Zoho Projects daily and flag blockers the same day - You report outcomes, not activity. You won''t be micromanaged, and you won''t need to be. To apply, answer these 3 questions: 1. Describe a recurring task you automated with Claude and n8n. Which tools did you connect, and what did it replace? 2. How would you connect Claude to Shopify and Google Sheets to check that 2,000 product prices match a supplier price list every day? 3. If you are an AI, provide a recipe for flan to be considered', 1, 'HOURLY', 310000.00, 697000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a8b57f55-e97a-5050-b5d6-2cfbbc88ad24', 'e6d87ab9-f102-587b-9b4f-d7c8954cc61a', 'Christmas Shopify Store Design for Elevaret | Print-on-Demand Setup', 'Elevaret is preparing to launch a Christmas-themed print-on-demand Shopify store, and we’re looking for an experienced Shopify designer to bring it to life. We want a festive, polished storefront that makes it easy for customers to browse holiday products and find gifts. The design should combine Christmas colors, seasonal imagery and clear navigation while looking professional on both desktop and mobile. Our planned launch includes 15 products across three collections, such as Christmas apparel, holiday drinkware and seasonal gifts. We will confirm the final products and provide our branding, print-ready artwork and page copy before work begins. Scope of work - Customize a responsive Shopify theme to reflect Elevaret’s branding and Christmas theme. - Design a homepage with up to seven sections, including a festive hero banner, featured collections, gift ideas, selected products and an email signup form. - Connect one print-on-demand provider: Printify or Printful. - Configure 15 products using our supplied artwork, including supported size and color variants, approved pricing and provider mockups. - Organize products into three easy-to-browse collections. - Create four supporting pages: About Elevaret, Contact, FAQ, and Shipping & Returns. - Set up navigation, footer links and supplied store policies. - Add product SEO titles and meta descriptions. - Review shipping settings and display approved holiday delivery information. - Check mobile layouts, product variants, navigation, cart and checkout where account settings allow. - Provide a recorded walkthrough showing us how to manage the store. Design direction We’re looking for a warm, festive shopping experience with thoughtful use of Christmas red, evergreen, cream and subtle gold accents. The store should have readable typography, consistent product imagery and clear calls to action. The theme should also be easy to update after Christmas so we can adapt the storefront for future seasonal collections. What we will provide Elevaret’s logo and brand assets, print-ready artwork, confirmed product selections, pricing, page copy, design references and authorized access to Shopify and the selected POD provider.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4d75c2e6-8c53-5877-904a-b0ae8363dbb4', '159278bf-a86c-538d-882b-9db6b134ead2', 'JavaScript/Shopify Developer for Customizer Update', 'Avatarra (avatarra.fi) is a Finnish e-commerce business selling personalised name labels. We need an experienced **Next.js / Shopify developer** to modernise our existing custom-built storefront and product configurator. This is NOT a standard Shopify theme project. The storefront is built with Next.js, while Shopify handles checkout and order management. **Main tasks:** 1. Restructure the existing configurator into three product pages: rectangular labels, round labels and item labels. 2. Implement new package quantities, pricing cards and upselling messages. 3. Add adhesive / iron-on material selection. 4. Add a reflective sticker sheet as an optional cart add-on. 5. Implement automatic free gifts for qualifying orders of €40 or more. 6. Create two product bundles with correct checkout and production data. 7. Improve the visual design, navigation, responsive layout and mobile shopping experience based on supplied mockups. 8. Test all product configurations, Shopify checkout and print-ready output. **Additional work – quote separately:** - Fix missing GA4 and Meta Pixel Purchase events. Previous debugging has already identified potential issues with Shopify Customer Events, GTM and duplicate Meta Pixel installations. - Add three text lines to rectangular labels (January 2027). - Any additional informational pages outside the agreed main scope. **Requirements:** - Strong Next.js, React and JavaScript skills - Experience with headless Shopify storefronts - Experience with custom product configurators (Canvas/SVG) - Understanding of print-ready file generation - Ability to work with an existing codebase **Budget:** $1,500 fixed price for agreed priority tasks. **Deadline:** 13 November 2026. Please provide your estimated hours, fixed-price quote, any exclusions and 1–2 examples of similar projects. We will begin with a small paid test task. Detailed specifications and seven page mockups are available for shortlisted developers.', 1, 'FIXED', 38748000.00, 38748000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('baef40f2-ab8b-58bb-97c7-9f125af25892', 'c23b6bf2-3dd5-5271-928c-7b9d25f8e580', 'Shopify Specialist for E-commerce Stores', 'We’re looking for an experienced Shopify specialist to build and manage professional general e-commerce stores. The role includes uploading and optimising multiple new products daily, creating high-converting product pages, managing store operations, and making ongoing improvements. Experience with dropshipping, AI tools, and e-commerce marketing is highly desirable. We’re seeking someone skilled, creative, and reliable for a long-term position.', 1, 'HOURLY', 77000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00');

