    updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at; Phase 3 is ongoing support. Roles (apply for one or more) 1. Senior Microsoft Access / VBA Developer: reverse-engineering and documenting complex Access applications (forms, queries, VBA, reports, linked tables). 10+ years of Access/VBA. 2. Business Analyst: requirements workshops with operational and finance users; construction, job costing or project accounting experience strongly preferred. 3. SQL Server / Data Engineer: data modelling, data quality, migration from Access back ends. 4. Solution Architect / Full-Stack Developer: rebuilding line-of-business apps on .NET/web or Power Platform; integration with ERP/accounting systems a plus. 5. QA / Test Analyst: test planning and reconciliation of financial outputs between old and new systems. Requirements - US-based (US time zones), fluent English, strong written communication. - Able to work under NDA with client data. - Examples of comparable work (describe your role; no client confidential details). Engagement Contract, part-time to full-time depending on phase. Start: discovery work is expected to begin in the coming weeks, subject to client award. We will interview shortlisted candidates now so the team is ready. To apply Tell us which role(s), your most relevant Access or modernization project, your availability over the next 3 months, and your hourly rate.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1937000.00, 2196000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('70179dd2-b49a-5aaa-b3a4-000535001a70', '05cd6334-8e84-5a89-9e5b-bf6b75cbd011', 'Smart Recovery managment tool', 'I need A smart recvoery application wich talk with MY ERP and and communciate with customer peridocy and and take input from user', 1, 'FIXED', 12916000.00, 12916000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('56f9190c-e70c-5601-bf44-642576f976bc', 'c70b94a3-744d-59ea-bb2e-01fe63ba560a', 'React Node.js Developer for Internal Automation', 'We need a developer to help automate internal sales and HR workflows for a growing company. The project will be built using React, Node.js, and Supabase, with a focus on improving efficiency and reducing manual tasks. You will work on building and refining internal tools that support day-to-day operations, collaborate with stakeholders to understand requirements, and help deliver a reliable solution that can scale with the business. Experience with similar automation projects and strong problem-solving skills are important for success.', 1, 'HOURLY', 517000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('3ed45fa7-4b30-500c-ae51-f4a8c48e8705', 'c92c1f05-a69b-5770-9d32-e52d8f7cedd7', 'Engineer-Developer for Sales Design Tool', 'We are a North American specialty construction materials manufacturer seeking an engineer-developer to convert design spreadsheets into a tested internal web app for sales. The tool will support preliminary design creation with engineer review, a deterministic calculation engine, Salesforce integration, and hosting in our Azure/M365 environment. You will collaborate closely with our engineers and Salesforce admin, with code maintained in our Azure DevOps repo. Phase 1 includes reviewing methods, meeting our engineer, and delivering a memo on architecture, integration, testing, MVP plan, cost, and knowledge transfer. Phase 2 involves building the tool based on Phase 1 scope. Required: civil/structural engineering degree, Python or C# with testing, Azure, Salesforce API, AI coding tools, and experience handing code to engineering teams. Apply with examples of tools you built and handed off, how you test calculations, your AI workflow, rate, and availability. NDA required. Company owns all work product.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1292000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('baec6229-df4c-59a8-8397-23ce9b2a34c5', '7e30ac56-3704-50a4-80d2-e7a090401366', 'Workflow specialist - Monday.com', 'Create a Monday.com workflow that automatically creates a record in Report B whenever a new record is added to Report A, and syncs all specified fields between the two reports in both directions. The workflow should also make calculated fields from Report B, such as Total Airfare Cost and Flight Credit Applied, visible to guests on Report A. Please address the limitation where mirror columns hide formulas from guests by using an alternative method to expose the calculated data clearly.', 1, 'HOURLY', 517000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('ffbcc742-987b-524a-b6f2-c65db1f261f5', '0793fa43-c951-5ffe-acc2-789d959589ce', 'Microsoft Access: Convert Contract Form to Auto-Sizing Report with PDF Export', 'We’re a construction contractor using a Microsoft Access database (.mdb, Access 2002-2003 format, opened in current Microsoft 365 Access) to produce customer contracts. The contract is currently built as a form. Its job description field is fixed-size, so long descriptions don’t fit, and we end up manually adjusting the layout in a PDF editor for every contract. We’d like this fixed properly. Scope: Convert the existing contract form into a report, keeping the current layout and branding. Make the job description (memo field) expand to fit its content and push all sections below it down the page. Keep the signature block together so it never splits across a page break. Always start the terms and conditions on their own page. Add a button on the data entry form that generates the report for the current record and saves it as a PDF named by contract number. Optional, priced separately: automatically reduce the font size when the job description exceeds a set length, so most contracts fit on one front page. What we’ll provide: A copy of the database with sample data only (no live customer records), plus screenshots of the current output and of the problem. Deliverables: The new report and any supporting VBA, delivered as objects we can import into our live database, with brief instructions for importing them. Requirements: Demonstrated experience with Access report design and VBA Fixed-price quote for items 1 through 5, with item 6 quoted separately Estimated turnaround time To apply, please answer briefly: How would you make a memo field expand on a report and push the content below it down, while keeping a terms and conditions section on its own page?', 1, 'FIXED', 10333000.00, 10333000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('995f5356-f47b-5af4-8c21-7216d59c727a', '5e510c0e-e4a3-5430-afe4-761a3a3d2d7e', 'Tuyển Freelancer trình bày các ứng dụng của Sharepoint web nội bộ', 'Hướng dẫn tính năng của sharepoint cho trang web intranet nội bộ của công ty', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 2000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('33593315-569a-5f8a-97bc-f22d3feafe34', '3bf3d1e4-c84d-5aa1-8033-3f385e9778f7', 'Vị trí: Frontend Developer(Remote)', 'Mô tả công việc Phát triển giao diện frontend cho hệ thống Chuyển thiết kế/Figma thành giao diện thực tế Kết nối API backend Tối ưu responsive cho desktop/tablet/mobile Tối ưu UX/UI để sản phẩm mượt, hiện đại, dễ dùng Phối hợp cùng backend để hoàn thiện flow sản phẩm ⸻ Yêu cầu Thành thạo React hoặc Next.js Thành thạo Tailwind CSS Có kinh nghiệm làm dashboard/web app Biết responsive tốt Có tư duy UI/UX hiện đại Biết dùng Git/GitLab Có trách nhiệm và chủ động trong công việc ⸻ Ưu tiên Có kinh nghiệm với: marketplace SaaS, platform CRM/dashboard Có portfolio sản phẩm thực tế Có khả năng tối ưu animation/micro interaction Biết TypeScript là lợi thế ⸻ Tech Stack React / Next.js Tailwind CSS REST API GitLab ⸻ Hình thức làm việc Remote linh hoạt Freelance theo module hoặc part-time dài hạn Thanh toán theo milestone/module', 1, 'FIXED', 5000000.00, 50000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('99607ed0-04e1-5f74-90ef-86058d65a113', 'd4abbc94-c89e-5b47-b07e-324e1374a543', 'REMOTE SUPPORT DEVELOPER PHP LARAVEL – CA TỐI', 'THÔNG TIN CÔNG VIỆC - Vị trí: Remote Support Developer (PHP Laravel – Ca tối) - Hình thức làm việc: Remote (Làm việc từ xa) - Thời gian làm việc: 20h00 – 22h30 (Từ Thứ 2 đến Chủ nhật) - Số lượng tuyển: 02 MÔ TẢ CÔNG VIỆC 1. Bảo trì & vận hành hệ thống nội bộ: - CRM / ERP / Zalo ZNS / Portal nội bộ / API / Các phần mềm khác khi có yêu cầu. - Theo dõi, kiểm tra và xử lý các lỗi phát sinh trong quá trình vận hành hệ thống. - Hỗ trợ kiểm tra log, phân tích nguyên nhân lỗi và đề xuất phương án xử lý. 2. Phát triển thêm tính năng - Tham gia phát triển các tính năng mới cho hệ thống hiện tại - Điều chỉnh, nâng cấp chức năng trên hệ thống có sẵn. - Tối ưu logic xử lý, database và API khi cần. 3. Xử lý sự cố kỹ thuật - Hỗ trợ xử lý các lỗi phát sinh trong quá trình hệ thống hoạt động. - Với các lỗi khẩn cấp ảnh hưởng đến vận hành hệ thống, ưu tiên hỗ trợ xử lý trong ngày nếu có thể (có thưởng nóng theo từng case). - Chủ động phối hợp để đảm bảo hệ thống hoạt động ổn định. YÊU CẦU ỨNG VIÊN - Có kiến thức hoặc kinh nghiệm làm việc với: PHP Laravel / Mysql / MariaDB / REST API / GIT - Có khả năng đọc hiểu source code có sẵn. - Có tư duy debug và xử lý lỗi. - Có trách nhiệm, chủ động trong công việc. - Cam kết làm việc đúng khung giờ 20h00 – 22h30 - Biết cơ bản về Linux Server. - Có kiến thức về deploy source code. - Đã từng làm CRM/ERP là lợi thế. - Có kinh nghiệm xử lý API, webhook, automation. - Đã từng làm việc remote. QUY TRÌNH LÀM VIỆC - Nhận task thông qua hệ thống quản lý công việc. - Báo cáo tiến độ và công việc cuối ca. - Toàn bộ source code quản lý bằng Git. - Không chỉnh sửa trực tiếp trên server production nếu chưa được xác nhận. THU NHẬP & QUYỀN LỢI - Lương cứng: 3.000.000 VNĐ/tháng - Thanh toán lương hàng tháng từ mùng 10 đến 15 của tháng - Thưởng nóng: Thưởng từ 100.000 – 500.000 VNĐ/case đối với: - Xử lý lỗi khẩn cấp cần support ngay. - Hỗ trợ ngoài khung giờ làm việc. - Hoàn thành tốt task phát sinh hoặc xử lý issue nhanh.', 1, 'FIXED', 2000000.00, 3000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('66bd40ea-512d-5d6e-9efb-bc0cb0049836', 'f169ea93-b3ab-530a-8644-be498d1ae0c2', 'Tuyển Frontend (Remote)', 'Mô tả công việc Phát triển giao diện frontend cho hệ thống Chuyển thiết kế/Figma thành giao diện thực tế Kết nối API backend Tối ưu responsive cho desktop/tablet/mobile Tối ưu UX/UI để sản phẩm mượt, hiện đại, dễ dùng Phối hợp cùng backend để hoàn thiện flow sản phẩm ⸻ Yêu cầu Thành thạo React hoặc Next.js Thành thạo Tailwind CSS Có kinh nghiệm làm dashboard/web app Biết responsive tốt Có tư duy UI/UX hiện đại Biết dùng Git/GitLab Có trách nhiệm và chủ động trong công việc ⸻ Ưu tiên Có kinh nghiệm với: marketplace SaaS, platform CRM/dashboard Có portfolio sản phẩm thực tế Có khả năng tối ưu animation/micro interaction Biết TypeScript là lợi thế ⸻ Tech Stack React / Next.js Tailwind CSS REST API GitLab ⸻ Hình thức làm việc Remote linh hoạt Freelance theo module hoặc part-time dài hạn Thanh toán theo milestone/module', 1, 'FIXED', 5000000.00, 50000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('aed6e40d-53b8-5ee7-b74d-73cd79121ac5', '74951f46-8290-586f-a2d7-860ca41fb566', 'IT Freelancer cứng mảng API / Webhook', 'Tiêu đề dự án: Tìm IT Freelancer cứng mảng API / Webhook kết nối hệ thống SaaS nước ngoài và cổng thanh toán tự động. Nội dung mô tả:Mình cần tìm 1 bạn IT Freelancer cứng tay (có kinh nghiệm làm về API, Webhook và các công cụ tự động hóa MMO) để triển khai dự án tối ưu hạ tầng cho hệ thống SaaS của doanh nghiệp. Ngân sách: 10.000.000đ – 15.000.000đ (Khoán việc theo tiến độ). Hình thức: Làm việc từ xa (Remote).Yêu cầu kỹ thuật chính:Kết nối API/Webhook giữa một nền tảng CRM quốc tế với cổng thanh toán tự động tại Việt Nam (như SePay/Casso) để tự động kích hoạt tài khoản khi có biến động số dư.Tối giản và tùy biến giao diện front-end của phần mềm (ẩn bớt tính năng thừa, bản địa hóa ngôn ngữ).Có kinh nghiệm cấu hình hạ tầng mạng, Proxy dân cư và VPS đám mây để chạy các tác vụ tự động hóa cơ bản. Lưu ý: Do dự án có tính bảo mật cao, ứng viên phù hợp bắt buộc phải ký Biên bản bảo mật thông tin (NDA) trước khi mình bàn giao tài khoản chủ và Briefing chi tiết công việc.', 1, 'FIXED', 10000000.00, 15000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('07e1edc3-1128-5cd8-b7c7-2c9cf01bc201', 'fc99f04b-5474-58f9-a118-92f9d0b13ea2', 'Hệ thống quản lý nội bộ chuỗi cung ứng', 'Cần tuyển Freelancer làm Zalo Mini App O2O đặt món + quản lý kho thô. Đã có sẵn tài liệu SRS chi tiết. Ngân sách: Thương lượng. Yêu cầu có kinh nghiệm làm Zalo Mini App Studio. Inbox nhận tài liệu', 1, 'FIXED', 12000000.00, 20000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f5ffe53c-af2b-5943-b004-75349f39a29f', 'f17c20fd-1ec0-5c65-8c70-24dfaa2a0ddf', 'Oracle OPERA / OHIP Developer Needed for Hotel Booking & Availability Platform', 'We are developing H Vibez, a hotel discovery and booking platform initially focused on hotels in Qatar. The platform is already under development, and we are looking for an experienced hospitality technology/API developer or company to help us complete the project, particularly the integration with Oracle OPERA PMS / OPERA Cloud. What We Need Our primary requirement is to retrieve real-time room availability and rates from multiple participating hotels using Oracle OPERA. We are currently exploring: Oracle Hospitality Integration Platform (OHIP) OPERA Cloud Distribution APIs Distribution Shop API OPERA Web Services (OWS) for hotels using older OPERA environments Multi-property hotel availability and rate searches Room/rate-plan mapping Eventually creating bookings directly into OPERA The goal is for a customer to search H Vibez using their check-in date, check-out date and number of guests, and receive live availability and pricing from participating hotels. Example: Customer → H Vibez → Oracle/Hotel PMS → Live Availability & Rates → H Vibez We do not want to build unnecessary PMS functionality from scratch if Oracle already provides the required functionality through OHIP/Distribution APIs. Who We''re Looking For We would particularly like to hear from developers/companies with proven experience in: Oracle OPERA Cloud / OPERA PMS OHIP REST APIs OPERA Cloud Distribution APIs / Shop APIs OWS/SOAP integrations Hotel booking engines, OTAs or channel managers Hotel PMS/API integrations Experience specifically with Oracle Hospitality is highly preferred. When applying, please briefly explain your previous OPERA/OHIP integration experience, which Oracle Hospitality APIs you have worked with, and how you would approach multi-hotel real-time availability for H Vibez. We are looking for someone who can first advise us on the correct architecture and Oracle integration approach, and then help us implement and complete the platform.', 1, 'FIXED', 51664000.00, 51664000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0af00c7b-d609-549a-b5aa-525e0e4bda33', 'c172a95f-3a27-56cb-9167-dc7091358f56', 'Senior Python/Django Backend Engineer – APIs, Domain Logic & Rules Engine', 'Project: Consumer Mobile Application Engagement: Freelance, hourly contract Duration: Initial 2 months, with potential for ongoing work Availability: 35-40 hours/week preferred, with regular overlap during Singapore business hours (GMT+8) ABOUT THE PROJECT Friday.social is a new kind of social calendar that helps friends turn plans into real-life experiences. Our mobile application combines social planning, messaging and AI-powered assistance. We’re building on an existing Python/Django backend and currently consolidating our architecture, simplifying APIs and establishing consistent domain rules ahead of launch. We’re looking for an experienced Backend Engineer to accelerate development of core functionality, working alongside our existing engineer and an experienced Technical Advisor. This is a hands-on implementation role requiring strong systems thinking, independent engineering judgment and the ability to deliver production-quality code. SCOPE OF WORK - Backend development: Build and integrate Python/Django services, RESTful APIs and PostgreSQL database operations against defined product use cases. - Domain rules & rules engine: Implement complex business logic, permissions, state transitions and application workflows within an agreed architecture, including building and integrating rules-engine components as specifications are finalised. - Integration & data integrity: Ensure consistent behaviour across backend services and APIs, with appropriate validation, transactions, authentication and authorisation. - Engineering quality: Write maintainable code with automated tests, systematic debugging, error handling and regression coverage. - Technical collaboration: Work with our Technical Advisor on architectural direction, collaborate with our existing Backend Engineer and proactively identify technical risks or dependencies. TECH STACK Core: Python, Django, Django REST Framework, PostgreSQL Supporting: Redis, Celery, ASGI/WebSockets Infrastructure & Integrations: Render, AWS S3, n8n WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR - Strong hands-on Python/Django, Django REST Framework and PostgreSQL experience. - Proven experience building, shipping and maintaining production backend systems. - Strong experience implementing complex domain models, business rules, permissions and state transitions, with consistent rule enforcement across backend services and APIs. - Solid understanding of API design, database transactions, data integrity and asynchronous processing. - Excellent debugging, automated testing and software engineering practices. - Ability to work independently within an existing architecture, communicate clearly and take ownership of deliverables. Nice to have: Domain-driven design, rule engines, Redis/Celery, WebSockets, social networking or scheduling applications, and AI/LLM integrations. We value demonstrated engineering capability over years of experience. Ideally, you’ll have 5+ years of relevant backend experience and a track record of delivering reliable production software. EXPECTED DELIVERABLES The engagement will involve: - Developing and integrating assigned backend APIs and functionality against agreed specifications. - Implementing and testing canonical domain rules and rules-engine components. - Resolving integration issues and ensuring consistent backend behaviour. - Delivering automated tests and concise technical documentation to support ongoing maintenance. - Work packages will be prioritised progressively as product specifications are finalised. TO APPLY Please share: - Relevant experience: Examples of Python/Django backend systems you’ve personally built or maintained in production. - Technical problem-solving: Briefly describe a complex business logic, state management or backend architecture problem you’ve solved, including your approach. - Availability: Your hourly rate, weekly availability and ability to overlap with Singapore business hours. We’re looking for someone who can contribute quickly, exercise sound engineering judgment and take ownership of delivering reliable backend functionality', 1, 'HOURLY', 258000.00, 387000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4f1c83ce-6823-516f-81c8-12d6b931e5c0', '5e032584-ed65-5635-b549-2bc90b63cd85', 'NestJS API returns 500 on GET /orders after deploy', 'We have a NestJS + Postgres API. After the last deploy, GET /orders returns 500 for logged-in users. Auth and other routes still work. Happens on staging with a small dataset. Need a root-cause fix, not a rewrite. Done when: 1. /orders returns the list for a valid JWT again 2. Error is handled cleanly if the query fails 3. Short note: what broke and what changed Stack: NestJS, TypeScript, Prisma, Postgres. Staging .env example included. I will share a zip of the project after hire.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b5b2c238-6924-50e8-91b7-c9d7bfb5f6d0', '0cc865f7-f02a-5d8e-a710-a6d9704732b5', 'Python Developer for Backend Development', 'We are seeking a Python developer to support backend development for a growing project. You will help build and maintain reliable backend systems, collaborate with the team, and contribute to scalable solutions. The ideal candidate is comfortable working in a dynamic environment and can help improve system performance and stability. This is a part-time opportunity with potential for long-term growth.', 1, 'HOURLY', 207000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e6be9f09-e206-5175-a682-8b29fd2c83d6', '6c7455ef-1686-5ff8-a394-bdc92b5939f2', 'Python FastAPI Developer – Fix/Build RESTful Endpoints or Microservice Task', 'We are Looking for an experienced Python backend engineer to handle a quick, well-defined FastAPI task. Budget: $40 (Fixed Price) Turnaround: 24–48 hours Scope of Work (One of the following): Implement or refactor 1–2 production-ready FastAPI endpoints with proper Pydantic schemas. Debug and resolve existing API performance issues, broken routes, or database query bottlenecks (SQLAlchemy/PostgreSQL). Set up a lightweight microservice boilerplate or integrate a third-party webhook/API with clean async handling. Requirements: Proven hands-on experience with Python 3.10+, FastAPI, and Pydantic. Strong grasp of asynchronous programming (async/await) and relational databases (PostgreSQL/SQLAlchemy). Clean code structure with proper error handling and auto-generated Swagger documentation. Fast communication and clear handoff/testing steps.', 1, 'FIXED', 1033000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f7d58cb9-ac0b-502a-92ff-cad0da0bdc73', 'f8533b34-d35b-5369-86dc-f877589fc378', 'BACKEND ENGINEER (NESTJS)', 'Mô tả công việc Tham gia phát triển và vận hành hệ thống backend quy mô lớn. Thiết kế và xây dựng REST API phục vụ Web, Mobile App Thiết kế database tối ưu hiệu năng và khả năng mở rộng. Phối...', 1, 'FIXED', 5000000.00, 50000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('c7e0b37f-c555-51ea-815d-48454f4239c9', '8067d2cd-df60-54bc-babf-b125f4579fe6', 'Next.js / Supabase developer to turn a working prototype into a production SaaS app', 'I have an existing web app built with Next.js and Supabase, hosted on Vercel. It is already in daily use. I''m looking for an experienced developer to review it and help turn it into a commercial SaaS product. Stage 1 (this job): - Review the existing code and point out issues with security, structure and performance - Recommend how to make it production-ready and usable by multiple businesses - Give a quote and timeline for the next stages You''ll need: - Strong Next.js, React and Supabase/PostgreSQL experience - Experience building and launching SaaS products - Experience integrating third-party APIs - Clear communication and some overlap with Australian business hours (AEST) To apply: - Links to 2–3 live apps you''ve built (Next.js/Supabase preferred) - A short description of the most similar project you''ve worked on - Start your proposal with the word "Ledgerline" so I know you''ve read this An NDA must be signed before any project details or code are shared. The budget is for Stage 1 only. Further stages will be quoted separately.', 1, 'FIXED', 38748000.00, 38748000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b49157bb-f9d3-59cf-80a6-d5bc53daac12', 'ec698fea-7d65-5126-96e8-5de17cce771d', 'Ui/UX Designer for B2B AI Saas platform', 'UI/UX Designer – B2B AI Software Platform (Contract/Freelance) We are looking for an experienced UI/UX Designer to help refine and redesign our existing AI-native enterprise software platform. Our platform is already developed and functional, but we want to significantly improve its usability, visual design, navigation, and overall user experience to make it intuitive, professional, and ready for commercial launch. Key Responsibilities: * Redesign and modernize the existing platform’s interface. * Simplify complex workflows and improve user navigation. * Create intuitive, clean, and visually appealing dashboards and interfaces. * Improve consistency across different modules and features. * Develop high-fidelity Figma designs and reusable UI components. * Collaborate with our developers to ensure smooth implementation. Requirements: * Proven experience designing SaaS, B2B, or enterprise software platforms. * Strong Figma skills and understanding of UX best practices. * Ability to simplify complex, feature-rich software. * Experience with AI-powered products, ERP, or CRM systems is a plus. * Portfolio demonstrating modern, user-friendly software interfaces. Project Type: Freelance / Contract, with potential for ongoing collaboration. To Apply: Please share your portfolio, relevant SaaS projects, availability, and estimated rates', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 904000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e7cf20d8-384d-5d0c-9cdc-a145a9a5b3c0', '52a45127-d887-542f-9b49-94e4fe2a9f31', 'B2B SaaS UX/UI & Creative Strategy Expert', 'B2B SaaS Creative Strategist & UX/UI Designer for Website Repositioning We''re looking for an experienced creative strategist and UX/UI designer to help us rethink how our software product communicates its value and connects with its target audience. This is an urgent project. We''re looking to select someone this week and begin as soon as possible. Budget: $1,000 to $1,500 Timeline: Approximately 1 to 2 weeks About the project We have an established software product for web designers and agencies. The product is functional and already has users, but we want to strengthen its positioning, storytelling, visual identity, and website conversion experience. We''re not looking for someone to simply make our website look better. We want a creative partner who can understand the business, challenge our assumptions, and translate research into a compelling digital experience. What we need 1. Market research and positioning Review our market, direct competitors, ideal customer profile, and current value proposition. Identify opportunities to communicate our differentiation more effectively and connect with the problems, motivations, and aspirations of our audience. 2. Creative strategy and storytelling Help refine our website narrative and information hierarchy. We want to move beyond communicating product features and create an experience focused on customer benefits, perceived value, and business outcomes. 3. Website UX/UI redesign Using the research and strategy, redesign two key marketing pages in Figma: • Homepage • Main product or pricing page We''re looking for strong visual direction, clear storytelling, thoughtful user journeys, persuasive layouts, and excellent responsive design. 4. Reusable design foundations Create a small, organized Figma component library covering typography, colors, spacing, buttons, cards, and reusable marketing sections. We want a foundation that our development team can extend. 5. Conversion recommendations Identify important UX and conversion opportunities and explain the reasoning behind your recommendations. We value designers who can connect creative decisions to business objectives. Expected deliverables • Concise market and competitor analysis • Positioning and messaging recommendations • Creative direction and visual references • Two responsive marketing page designs in Figma • Reusable Figma components and design foundations • Prioritized UX and conversion recommendations • Final walkthrough and developer handoff Who we''re looking for You should have experience with B2B SaaS, digital products, or conversion-focused marketing websites. We''re particularly interested in professionals who combine: • UX research and business understanding • Brand positioning and creative strategy • Strong visual design and storytelling • Conversion-focused UX/UI • Advanced Figma skills • Clear communication and independent thinking We already have development capabilities, so this is primarily a research, strategy, and design engagement. How to apply Please share: 1. Two or three relevant projects, preferably B2B SaaS or software marketing websites. 2. Your specific role and contribution to each project. 3. A brief explanation of how you approach research before design. 4. An example where your creative decisions helped solve a business or communication problem. 5. Your availability to start and estimated delivery timeline. We prefer thoughtful, personalized proposals over generic portfolios. We''re looking for someone who brings a strong point of view, asks the right questions, and can turn complex products into simple, distinctive digital experiences.', 1, 'FIXED', 38748000.00, 38748000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('c0a71ab5-f69c-56d4-bcc5-841f684bb3ee', '7e1a9e89-1a49-57f7-9587-07331596c521', 'Thuê lập trình viên Fullstack xây dựng website bán quần áo bằng Svelte và Go', 'Mục tiêu: Xây dựng một website bán quần áo hoàn chỉnh bao gồm cả giao diện người dùng (Frontend) và hệ thống quản trị (Backend). Phạm vi và đầu ra: - Phát triển Frontend sử dụng framework Svelte để đảm bảo tốc độ tải trang nhanh và trải nghiệm mượt mà. - Phát triển Backend sử dụng ngôn ngữ Go để xử lý dữ liệu hiệu quả và ổn định. - Xây dựng cơ sở dữ liệu lưu trữ sản phẩm, đơn hàng và thông tin khách hàng. - Bàn giao toàn bộ mã nguồn trên Git và tài liệu hướng dẫn cài đặt, vận hành hệ thống. Yêu cầu phù hợp: - Có kinh nghiệm thực chiến với Svelte và Go. - Đã từng triển khai các dự án thương mại điện tử hoặc web bán hàng. - Có tư duy tốt về thiết kế cơ sở dữ liệu và tối ưu hóa hiệu năng. Tiêu chí nghiệm thu: - Website vận hành ổn định, không có lỗi nghiêm trọng trên các trình duyệt phổ biến. - Các luồng chính như xem sản phẩm, thêm vào giỏ hàng và đặt hàng hoạt động chính xác. - Mã nguồn được viết sạch, có comment rõ ràng và dễ bảo trì.', 1, 'FIXED', 500000.00, 1000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('80565a9f-ec20-55f4-b3e3-4e5b2bde7d1b', '813728ac-dd06-5f44-8d66-89598689d186', '[freelance] cần tìm developer làm web app thi thử IELTS + Cambridge cho học sinh (budget 20tr)', 'dự án: Trung tâm Anh ngữ JYS English (Nghe An) cần tìm một bạn Developer (freelance) để xây dựng hệ thống thi thử trực tuyến cho học sinh. Ngân sách: 20,000,000 VNĐ (Trọn gói). yêu cầu chính: 1. Hỗ trợ 2 định dạng đề thi: * IELTS: Có đầy đủ Reading, Listening (đồng bộ audio), Writing (có bộ đếm giờ) và tính điểm tự động. * Cambridge (Starters/Movers/Flyers): Bắt buộc hỗ trợ câu hỏi dạng hình ảnh (ví dụ: nhìn tranh chọn True/False, nối tranh với từ vựng). 2. Trang quản trị (Backend) siêu dễ dùng: * Giáo viên bên mình không rành công nghệ, nên cần tính năng "Quick Upload". * Yêu cầu: Upload đề thi qua file Excel/Word mẫu hoặc giao diện nhập liệu cực kỳ đơn giản (không bắt giáo viên vào admin phức tạp). 3. Trải nghiệm học sinh: * Giao diện Mobile-friendly (tối ưu cho phụ huynh/học sinh dùng điện thoại). * Tốc độ tải trang nhanh, ổn định. 4. Integration: * Chạy trên subdomain (ví dụ: test.jysenglish.com). giải pháp kỹ thuật: Ưu tiên các giải pháp Nhanh - Gọn - Nhẹ. Các bạn có thể đề xuất dùng WordPress (LMS Plugin), Code thuần (PHP/Laravel) hoặc Customize source code có sẵn. Miễn sao sản phẩm cuối cùng ổn định và dễ dùng cho giáo viên. cuối cùng, bạn sẽ quyết định sử dụng những công cụ nào để thực hiện việc này. cách ứng tuyển: Vui lòng nhắn tin trực tiếp qua Messenger cho mình các thông tin sau: 1. Công nghệ/Technical Stack bạn dự định dùng. 2. Giải pháp của bạn để giúp giáo viên upload đề thi nhanh nhất (quan trọng). 3. Demo các sản phẩm tương tự (nếu có).', 1, 'FIXED', 15000000.00, 20000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('7c5ac9ff-3b22-5dd1-88c2-d266297331d1', '9137a828-9f6a-5a3d-a7db-440243a3c4cd', 'Full Stack AI developer for fashion SaaS MVP', 'We’re looking for a skilled Full Stack AI Developer to build an MVP for an innovative fashion SaaS platform. The ideal candidate has experience with frontend and backend development, AI/LLM integration, API development, and database management. You’ll be responsible for developing scalable features, integrating AI-powered fashion solutions, and delivering a user-friendly, high-performance product. Experience with modern frameworks, cloud deployment, and SaaS applications is a plus. We’re looking for someone proactive who can turn ideas into a functional MVP efficiently.', 1, 'FIXED', 387000.00, 387000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('7fae8bb1-c5a8-5158-a3d7-9ec6e93a3d90', '54be904b-be57-56ed-877c-6eafd31077ac', 'Audit Existing Web App and Add Secure Payment Feature', 'About the Project We have an existing web application that is already live in some form, but it needs a technical review before we add a payment feature. The immediate goal is to understand the current codebase, identify any security or UX issues, and then implement a reliable payments flow. If the first phase goes well, there may be ongoing support and development work. What We Need First I’m looking for a developer who can review the current web app and provide a practical audit, not just a high-level opinion. The audit should cover: - Code quality and structure - User authentication and account security - Existing backend/API setup - Frontend issues affecting user experience - Any obvious bugs, performance issues, or scalability concerns - Recommendations before adding payments Payment Feature After the audit, we want to add a secure payment flow. The exact payment provider can be discussed, but Stripe is likely preferred. The feature may include checkout, payment status handling, error states, confirmation screens, and backend validation through secure API integration. Technical Context The app uses web technologies and may involve JavaScript on the frontend and Python on the backend. I need someone comfortable working with an existing codebase, reviewing REST APIs, improving authentication flows, and making UI/UX adjustments where needed. Deliverables - Initial technical audit with clear findings - Recommended plan for payment implementation - Secure payment integration - Testing of payment and user flows - Documentation of changes made - Suggestions for ongoing maintenance and support To Apply Please include: - Examples of web apps you have worked on - Your experience with JavaScript, Python, and API development - Any Stripe or payment integration experience - What you would review first in an existing app takeover - Your availability and whether you can provide ongoing support Please start your reply with the word AUDIT so I know you read the full post.', 1, 'FIXED', 18082000.00, 18082000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('42067936-95d3-5af8-ac5f-0296a2e6373e', '5872fdbd-b980-574a-9721-e6ff176cd928', 'Full-Stack Developer | React/Next.js, Node.js, Python & GPT API', 'Looking for a skilled full-stack developer to implement features in an existing application using modern development practices and AI-assisted coding tools. Project Scope: * Frontend: React.js / Next.js for the web interface. * Node.js Backend: API development and request handling. * Python Service: Crawling and extracting data from third-party sources. * AI Integration: Integrate the GPT API into the Python crawler service for AI-powered data processing and extraction. Requirements: * Strong experience with React.js/Next.js, Node.js, and Python. * Hands-on experience integrating OpenAI GPT APIs. * Extensive use of AI coding tools to accelerate development, debugging, and testing. * Experience with REST APIs, web crawling, and third-party integrations. This is a focused implementation project with potential for ongoing collaboration. Please share relevant work and your estimated timeline when applying.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('d4c0eabb-5a01-56dd-bd37-e618a5b7eb54', '001ee12e-b1dd-53bc-83f4-530da9a88368', 'Meta / Facebook App Review & Graph API setup specialist (Pages publishing SaaS)', 'We run a live, fully built SaaS that lets businesses schedule and publish posts to the Facebook Pages they manage (Facebook only). Privacy policy, terms, data deletion pages and callbacks are already live. Our Meta Business portfolio is already Business Verified and verified as a Tech Provider. What we need: 1. Written setup plan for a Business-type app with Facebook Login for Business and Advanced Access for pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, pages_manage_engagement, pages_read_user_content, read_insights and business_management. 2. Create and configure the app inside our business portfolio (we add you with limited access) and run a successful test call for each permission. 3. Reviewer access instructions and one screencast per permission. 4. Use-case text per permission and data-handling answers. Submit, handle feedback (2 resubmissions included), then hand over. No coding needed. No password sharing or borrowed accounts. Product details and access are shared after hire. Done when: - A written setup plan is delivered and approved by us before any app is created. - The app exists inside our business portfolio, is configured (domains, URLs, icon, callbacks, Require App Secret, Login for Business configuration), and has a logged successful API call for each permission. - One screencast per permission (1080p, English, no audio) shows login, consent, the feature and the result on Facebook, and we approve the full review package before submission. - The submission is made from our app, Meta''s feedback is handled (up to 2 resubmissions), and every Meta message is shared with us word for word. - Handover: a configuration list (no secrets in chat), screencast files, final submission text, the list of approved permissions, and a list of ongoing obligations. Then your business access is removed. Paid by fixed-price milestones: (1) setup plan, (2) app configuration and test calls, (3) review package approved by us, (4) submission, feedback and handover. Approval is Meta''s decision; we pay for the documented work. Optional small retainer for upkeep after approval.', 1, 'FIXED', 12916000.00, 12916000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('309ddc4c-f999-51f9-86de-33b86c97bcc0', 'd1679bcc-f6dc-5b4c-b596-497a57d7c503', 'Arabic-speaking full-stack Django/React developer (Full-time)', 'We are an edutech company building software that teaches Arabic to both native and non-native speakers. Our mission is to spread Arabic — the language of the Quran — around the world, and to make it easier for everyone to learn and understand. We''re a mission-driven team in an exciting growth phase. With several successful projects behind us, we''re expanding and building a new squad to take our work further. The Product You''ll be working on an existing platform designed to help Arabic students strengthen their language skills. It helps students achieve higher marks in their Arabic exams and gives parents a way to help their children grow to love and improve their Arabic. The product is small-scale today, but our ambitions are high. Exciting features are on the roadmap, including a customized flipbook with voice detection and student reading correction, and personalized assessments of each student''s strengths and weaknesses. Your Role We''re looking for a Senior Full Stack Developer (5+ years) to join our squad as a hands-on individual contributor. You''ll report to the Tech Lead and Team Lead, and work as one of two full-stack engineers on the team, alongside a UI/UX designer, QA, and business analyst. This is a backfill role, and we''re hiring as soon as possible. What You''ll Do - Build and enhance new features across the full stack, using Django and React - Write clean, maintainable, well-tested code, including unit tests - Own features end-to-end, from understanding written specifications through coding, testing, and delivery - Work effectively within a large existing codebase, getting up to speed quickly and respecting established patterns - Research and evaluate third-party services and libraries independently, weighing their trade-offs and impact on the rest of the codebase - Contribute to challenging upcoming features such as voice detection and personalized student assessments - Participate in Agile ceremonies including daily stand-ups, and communicate clearly with the tech lead, team lead, and wider squad What We''re Looking For Must-haves - 5+ years of professional full-stack development experience - Strong proficiency with Django (Python) on the backend - Solid experience with React on the frontend - Experience with MySQL and Redis - Comfortable building and consuming REST APIs - Familiarity with Docker and cloud environments - Ability to write unit tests as a matter of habit - Able to quickly grasp new technologies and do your own research - Capable of assessing the pros and cons of a given library or service and its effects on the wider system - A highly effective communicator with strong logical-thinking skills - Team-oriented, even when working independently - Open to feedback from the team and tech leads, and eager to keep growing Values & mindset We''re a mission-driven company, and we''re looking for someone whose values align with ours. You should feel genuinely connected to our mission of spreading and teaching Arabic, and thrive in a culture rooted in that purpose. We want someone ambitious, motivated, resilient in the face of new challenges, and easy to work with. What Success Looks Like In this role, we''ll measure you on a combination of velocity, quality, and ownership. A great hire is easy to work with, embraces new challenges without giving up, produces high-quality work that follows specifications, accepts feedback with an open heart, and communicates clearly while staying motivated by our mission. Interview Process Our process typically takes 1–2 weeks and consists of: - CV screening - HR interview - Technical interview - Team & Tech Lead interview', 1, 'HOURLY', 155000.00, 194000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('80544a24-cae6-5789-bd14-fe159cb395af', '76bf1e61-283e-5667-9378-e55d9c05cb41', 'Build a Gamified Eco-Tracker Web App', 'Overview We are looking for a developer to quickly build "Greenie," a responsive web app that encourages sustainable habits through a gamified eco-action tracker. The estimated effort is 8 to 12 hours, with a total fixed budget of $100 USD. Key Features to Develop : The app requires user authentication for account creation and login with an email, password, and user profile. You will build an action logging interface to record eco-actions from a configurable JSON file, applying fixed points and respecting daily limits. Gamification elements include automated tracking of daily streaks, total points, and points earned today. For social features and leaderboards, users must be able to search for other students, use a follow/unfollow system, and view two weekly leaderboards for the Global Top 20 and Following. Additional pages include a personal history log showing the last 20 entries and a static "Which bin in Zürich?" info guide driven by a JSON file. Tech Stack & Deployment For the front-end, you may use your choice of mainstream technology, though open-source is preferred. The back-end and database must run on a free-tier managed service. Supabase is our preferred option, but alternatives can be proposed in your bid. The front-end must be served as static files, such as via GitHub Pages, with zero running costs. Code must be maintained from day one in a shared GitHub repository complete with seed data and a comprehensive README. Timeline & Milestones This is an urgent timeline starting ASAP. Milestone 1 accounts for 50% of the payment and is due Saturday, Oct 31, 2026. It focuses on registration, login, home status, action logging, daily streaks, and the deployed skeleton. Milestone 2 accounts for the remaining 50% and is due Friday, Nov 6, 2026, focusing on leaderboards, the following system, the info guide, remaining features, and final handover. Freelancer Expectations You must build exactly against the provided Figma mock-up, ensuring a mobile-first design responsive down to 360 px width. You are required to meet all acceptance criteria outlined in the provided brief and provide a short written update every two days. Any use of AI coding assistants must be declared milestone-by-milestone. To Apply Please review the attached Greenie_Requirements.pdf for full user stories, acceptance criteria, and technical constraints before submitting your proposal. Let us know what frontend framework you plan to use and confirm your ability to meet the milestone dates.', 1, 'FIXED', 2583000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('6353d6f3-37d3-5d02-80c8-99d8e664f770', 'c25c94d1-229f-5401-9e56-391b0c797864', 'Senior Full-Stack React/Node.js Developer to Assess, fix and launsch existing App', 'We are looking for an experienced Senior Full-Stack Developer to troubleshoot,fix,inprove and evaluate NEXUS for launch, an existing family-management application, we prefer to improve existing code rather than rebuild, not just an audit. Current technology: * Frontend: React / Vite * Backend: Node.js / Express * Database: MySQL / Drizzle ORM * Intended platforms: iOS and Android Known issues requiring investigation: * Recurring tasks and appointments do not consistently appear in the schedule. * Push notifications and reminders are not functioning reliably. * Some information is not saved or updated correctly. * Certain editing functions do not work as expected. * Mobile compatibility, reliability, and deployment readiness need evaluation. Deliverables for the initial audit: 1. Review the existing codebase and application architecture. 2. Identify the causes of the reported problems. 3. Assess the application’s readiness for iOS and Android deployment. 4. Provide a written report identifying critical issues and recommended solutions. 5. Provide an estimated timeline and fixed-price proposal for completing the repairs and preparing the app for launch. 6. Implement and test agreed priority fixes within the initial three hundred scope. Developer requirements: Strong experience with React, Node.js, Express, MySQL, debugging existing applications, and mobile push notifications. We are looking for someone who can improve our existing application rather than rebuild it from scratch. Clear communication in English, transparency about costs, and experience taking applications through testing and launch are essential. Budget: Initial budget 300 dollars; covers initial diagnosis plus agreed priority fixes; additional work only by a separate quote. Potential follow-up: If the assessment is satisfactory, we may offer a separate contract for repairs, testing, launch, and ongoing maintenance.', 1, 'FIXED', 7750000.00, 7750000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b48f8bbe-8b1c-5426-bf71-dfca0a284ebe', 'ebc982cb-42e6-5211-878f-d7b35bcbd8cf', 'Full-Stack Next.js 15 & Node.js Developer', 'Looking for an expert Full-Stack Developer to modernize our existing agency platform. The work includes migrating the frontend from CSR to Next.js with SSG/ISR, addressing critical security issues, replacing db.json with MongoDB, and deploying the application using Docker while preserving all animations and user experience. The ideal freelancer should be able to improve performance, enhance security, and ensure a smooth transition with minimal disruption to the current platform.', 1, 'FIXED', 20666000.00, 20666000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('48a1b22b-351d-5dcf-a42f-903bd184a2e5', '15438dc9-414f-5e10-956b-c001ec51ec15', 'Fast Full-Stack Developer (Next.js / Node / MongoDB), AI-Native (Claude Code / Codex)', 'Description: PAAW (paaw.co) is an AI-powered pet adoption marketplace live in the US and France, with 145K+ monthly visitors and 3,600+ shelter partners. Speed is our #1 criterion. We’re looking for a developer who ships fixes and changes in hours, not days, by working daily with Claude Code, Codex or Cursor. If AI agents aren’t at the core of how you code, this isn’t the right fit. Our stack: Frontend: Next.js (App Router, SSR/ISR), React Backend: Node.js, Firebase (Auth + Cloud Functions), AWS Database: MongoDB Atlas Payments: Stripe (checkout, paid contacts) Transactional email: Postmark; marketing email: Brevo Maps & location: Google Maps API, LocationIQ / Stadia Maps AI: OpenAI / Claude APIs (Oscar, our matching engine) Analytics: Google Analytics, Looker Studio What we need: Very fast turnaround on bugs and site changes An AI-native workflow: Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, every day Speed with care: you test before shipping, especially emails and Stripe flows Same-day communication when something breaks Nice to have: marketplace experience, Postmark or Stripe webhooks, SEO on Next.js. The detailed task list will be shared with shortlisted candidates. To apply, answer: - Describe your AI coding workflow (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor): what you delegate to agents, and what you check yourself. - What is the fastest you’ve shipped a production fix? Walk us through it. - A production incident you handled: how you found it and how you prevented it from happening again. - Your experience with Stripe checkout and webhooks. - Your availability this week and your hourly rate.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1033000.00, 2196000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('effa31ee-8fc0-5110-9047-0fe19470dda4', '54f08a3d-342e-530c-8bda-25ce2438fe60', 'Next.js Developer for Website Build', 'I’m looking for a Next.js developer who already owns a Tailwind Plus license to build my 5-page company website using the “Studio” template. The design should remain exactly as provided, and the final deliverable must be a private GitHub repository. This is a fixed-price project with a budget of $200 and a 5-day delivery timeline.', 1, 'FIXED', 5166000.00, 5166000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('2feb146e-21b9-59be-bf6e-e7362e6eff1d', '132e0502-a6b1-54d0-a818-a30e0bb2bfa8', 'Senior Flutter Full Stack Engineer (Long-Term Product Position)', 'We’re looking for an experienced Flutter engineer to join our team full-time and help build a rapidly growing SaaS platform used by service businesses across North America. This is not a short-term freelance project. We’re looking for someone who wants to become part of the team for years, not weeks. You’ll work directly with the founders, the development team, and help build software that thousands of businesses rely on every day. What You’ll Work On Our platform includes: * Flutter Mobile (iOS & Android) * Flutter Web * Customer Portal * Scheduling & Dispatching * CRM * Estimates & Invoicing * Payment Processing * AI-powered features * Maps & GPS * Customer Messaging * Reporting & Analytics * Internal business tools You’ll spend your time: * Building new features * Improving existing functionality * Fixing bugs * Optimizing performance * Maintaining backend services and APIs * Reviewing architecture and suggesting improvements * Working closely with our team to continually improve the product ⸻ Required Experience We’re looking for someone who has: * 4+ years of professional Flutter development * Experience shipping production Flutter applications * Strong backend development experience * Firebase * SQL database experience * Authentication & authorization * Git version control * Experience debugging large production applications * Excellent written and spoken English Bonus Experience Experience with any of the following is a plus: * SaaS applications * AWS * Stripe or other payment processors * Google Maps * Push Notifications * AI integrations * Large production codebases ⸻ What We’re Looking For We value engineers who: * Take ownership of their work * Write clean, maintainable code * Think through problems before jumping into solutions * Communicate well * Get things done quickly * Care about building great software * Want a long-term opportunity instead of constantly switching projects ⸻ Please Answer These Questions To help us evaluate applicants, please answer the following in your proposal: 1. How many years have you worked professionally with Flutter? 2. Please send 2–3 examples of production apps you’ve personally built. 3. Describe your backend experience. 4. What databases have you worked with? 5. Tell us about the most technically challenging feature you’ve built. 6. Tell us about a bug that took multiple days to solve. What was causing it, and how did you eventually fix it? 7. Have you worked on a SaaS product before? If so, tell us about it. 8. What time zone are you in? 9. Are you available full-time? 10. Why are you looking for a long-term position? ⸻ Important To show you’ve read this posting carefully, begin your proposal with the words: Blue Rocket Applications that don’t begin with these words won’t be considered. ⸻ We’re looking for someone who wants to build something meaningful over the long term. If that sounds like you, we’d love to hear from you.', 1, 'HOURLY', 465000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('8ebdc1ac-0c48-510d-a9b6-8cf57d0b1f15', 'f24e1ab3-48e5-505c-b8a7-ae00463fd035', 'Mid-Level / Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer (Python, React, Next.js, AI) — Long-Term Opportunity', 'Experience Level: Mid-Level / Senior (4+ Years) Budget: $2,000–$4,000 USD per project Project Type: Ongoing / Long-Term Collaboration Client Location: Florida, USA Work Arrangement: Remote About the Opportunity We are looking for a skilled and reliable Mid-Level or Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer to work on software development projects for a US-based client in Florida. The ideal candidate has strong backend and frontend development experience, excellent problem-solving abilities, and the communication skills needed to collaborate effectively with an international team. We are looking for someone who can contribute to real-world projects, take ownership of assigned responsibilities, and build a long-term professional relationship with our team. Required Qualifications At least 4 years of professional software development experience. Strong proficiency in Python, particularly Django and FastAPI. Solid experience with JavaScript and TypeScript. Hands-on frontend development experience with React and Next.js. Strong knowledge of SQL and NoSQL databases, such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, and MongoDB. Experience with AI-powered applications, including LLMs, RAG, or related AI integrations. Experience developing and integrating RESTful APIs. Familiarity with Git, testing, debugging, and clean coding practices. Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively with a development team. English Communication Clear and professional English communication is essential for this role. B2 English proficiency is the minimum requirement. C1 proficiency is strongly preferred. C2 proficiency is a significant advantage. Comfortable participating in technical discussions, video meetings, and regular project updates. Availability for reasonable working-hour overlap with US Eastern Time. Nice-to-Have Skills Experience with the following technologies is a bonus, but not mandatory: Angular or Vue.js Java / Spring Boot C# / .NET Ruby on Rails AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Docker, Kubernetes, and CI/CD Vector databases, AI agents, or advanced LLM integrations Key Responsibilities Develop and maintain scalable full-stack web applications. Build backend APIs and services using Python, Django, and FastAPI. Implement responsive frontend interfaces using React, Next.js, and TypeScript. Design, manage, and optimize SQL and NoSQL databases. Integrate third-party services and AI-powered functionality. Collaborate with the US-based client to understand requirements and deliver practical solutions. Troubleshoot issues, improve application performance, and maintain code quality. Provide clear progress updates and meet agreed project milestones. Compensation & Engagement Budget: $2,000–$4,000 USD per project. Compensation depends on project scope, complexity, and experience. Project-based engagement with potential for continuous work. Long-term collaboration opportunities for candidates who demonstrate strong technical skills, communication, and reliability. How to Apply Please include the following in your proposal: A brief introduction and your total years of professional experience. Your experience with Python, Django, FastAPI, React, Next.js, and TypeScript. Examples of projects involving AI, LLMs, or RAG, if applicable. Your GitHub, portfolio, or relevant project links. Your English proficiency level (B2, C1, or C2). Your availability and ability to overlap with US Eastern Time. We value developers who are proactive, dependable, technically capable, and comfortable communicating directly with clients. If you''re a Mid-Level or Senior Software Engineer looking for challenging projects and a long-term opportunity with a US-based client, we''d love to hear from you.', 1, 'HOURLY', 646000.00, 1162000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('c3cdd4ca-20ac-51f1-b9d7-fa48e2a8440c', '9ac01189-17b1-586f-8dcf-d3270b7fed82', 'Full-stack developer to turn a working front-end demo into a live MVP (Supabase, Arabic/English RTL)', 'Title: Full-stack developer to turn a working front-end demo into a live MVP (Supabase, Arabic/English RTL) Hi, I''m building a two-sided marketplace platform in Saudi Arabia that connects event companies with event workers and service providers (hosts, photographers, DJs, coordinators). I already have a fully working front-end demo (vanilla JavaScript PWA, Arabic/English with RTL, mobile-first) that uses localStorage and fake data. The UI, design and all Arabic/English text are done. I need the real back end and a live launch. Scope (about 25 screens, all already designed in the demo): - Public: landing, login, sign up, account recovery (4) - Worker / service provider: home, opportunities, opportunity detail, my applications, inbox, profile, portfolio, settings (8) - Company: home, my events, create event (multi-step), applicants, inbox, company profile, settings (7) - Admin: users, company approval, listings, reports, basic stats (5) What I need: 1. Real accounts: phone-number login with OTP for worker, provider and company, plus a simple admin role. 2. A real database and file storage (I suggest Supabase, but I''m open to your recommendation) to replace the localStorage data layer. 3. Profiles with role, nationality, languages, city, photo and a small portfolio. 4. Companies post opportunities; matching workers (role + nationality + ALL required languages + city) get notified. 5. Applications, accept/reject, backup list, and in-app chat. 6. Server-side blocking of phone numbers (digits and spelled-out numbers), emails, links and social handles in messages and listings. This must run on the server, not in the browser. 7. Notifications (in-app plus WhatsApp or email). 8. Admin panel to approve companies, remove users or listings, and see basic stats. 9. Deployment on my own domain, backups, and basic security (row-level security, rate limiting). Out of scope for the MVP: online payments, paid plans, live-event replacement flow. I will provide, after we agree: the demo source code and link, a written requirements document (screens, fields, rules) and the Arabic/English text. Requirements: - Experience with Supabase or Firebase, and vanilla JS or a lightweight front-end. - Experience with Arabic/RTL products is a strong plus. - Experience with OTP/SMS in Saudi Arabia (or willingness to integrate a local provider) is a plus. Please reply with: - Two similar projects you''ve shipped (links that work). - Your proposed stack, a fixed price with a milestone breakdown, and a realistic timeline. - How you would implement the server-side blocking of contact details. - What you need from me to start. - Confirmation that all code, accounts, and the domain will be owned by me at delivery (written IP assignment). - How long you provide free bug fixes after delivery. I will review and accept each milestone before payment. Communication in English or Arabic is fine. Thank you.', 1, 'FIXED', 154992000.00, 154992000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('47eeb91e-99a4-56d4-9a32-9c3a0c08e7fb', '014e9d8d-d087-5308-9f35-fddfc89a2b2b', 'Senior Full-Stack Software Developer | App Developer', 'We want someone who can take an idea and turn it into something amazing. Someone who combines outstanding technical ability with exceptional visual design skills and knows how to use AI to develop software faster and smarter. We’re not looking for average. We’re looking for exceptional. Beautiful software matters. We believe great applications should be as impressive to look at as they are to use. You need an exceptional eye for design, a genuine understanding of UI/UX and the ability to create modern, polished applications that people love using. The little details matter. Layout, typography, colours, responsiveness and the overall user experience should be second nature to you. We want someone who takes pride in every aspect of their work and won’t settle for something that’s simply good enough. AI is changing development. You should be leading the way. We’re looking for someone who is already highly experienced with AI development tools such as Claude Code, Cursor and other emerging technologies. You should be a strong full-stack developer, capable of independently designing, building and deploying complete web and mobile applications. More importantly, you should know how to combine your own expertise with AI to dramatically accelerate development while maintaining exceptional standards. We want to turn ideas into working applications quickly, without compromising quality. Our culture is important to us. At REA, our purpose is to inspire positive change to a sustainable future. Our culture is built around five values: Ownership, Passionate, Exceeding Expectations, Collaboration and Sustainable. We believe in owning what we do, getting things done and putting solutions first. We’re passionate about our work, curious about new ideas and always looking for ways to exceed expectations. We collaborate, share feedback, support each other and believe that learning and improving never stops. Our standards are non-negotiable. We’re looking for someone who genuinely connects with these values and wants to be part of a team that lives by them. Why join REA? This is a long-term, full-time position, working remotely from the Philippines or India as part of our Australian team. You’ll work directly with our management team, helping design and develop new applications that support our business and future growth. You’ll have the opportunity to influence how we build our technology, explore emerging AI tools and take real ownership of your projects. We’re looking for someone who wants more than just another development job. We want someone who is excited about building great things and growing with us. Show us what you’ve built. We’re more interested in your ability than your qualifications. We’d love to see examples of applications you’ve personally designed and developed, particularly those demonstrating exceptional visual design, user experience and technical quality. Tell us how you’re using AI to accelerate your development and what makes your work stand out. Please include your portfolio, relevant experience and expected monthly salary. If you’re passionate about building beautiful software, love solving problems and believe in exceeding expectations, we’d love to hear from you.', 1, 'FIXED', 12916000.00, 12916000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('3a7136b5-b724-5b9e-a628-fb9c8e0cd950', '8b54d72d-dce9-54ee-beae-fdee290f52ce', 'Custom Perfume Ordering Web App', 'Please quote a simple web app with two screens: one for customers on their phones and one for staff on a desktop. Customer screen Customers scan a QR code and: 1. Enter their name, phone and email. 2. Select ingredients from list 3. Assign percentages totaling 100%. of the ingredients 4. Choose a strength setting. 5. Name their product and submit it. Staff screen The submission appears on the desktop. Staff can: - View and adjust the selections, percentages and strength. - See automatically calculated quantities for a test sample and a full-size product. - Save the final approved formula under the customer’s profile. - Copy the product name for label printing. - Generate a printable card with a QR code linking to that saved product. Reordering and email The customer receives a thank-you email with their saved product and reorder link. Scanning the card or clicking the link lets them request another bottle in an available size. Staff receives the request. Basic administration We need to edit ingredients, sizes, prices and strength settings, and search customer records and saved formulas. Changes to ingredients must not overwrite previously saved formulas. For this quote, exclude payment processing, shipping integration and automatic printer integration. Please provide your fixed price, estimated delivery time, monthly running costs and any questions or exclusions.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 904000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('27047d83-5b4b-5c92-8575-fc838de12a54', 'ce23b934-4849-5bd1-bc1a-1d82d9601f37', 'Senior Full-Stack Agency Needed for AI-Powered Mobile + Web SaaS Platform', 'We are looking for an experienced software development agency to build a scalable AI-powered SaaS platform that includes: Web application Mobile application AI-powered automation features Backend APIs and infrastructure This is a long-term project with multiple phases and ongoing development opportunities. The platform will focus on workflow automation, customer management, scheduling, AI assistance, analytics, and real-time operational tools for service-based businesses. We are specifically looking for an agency with proven expertise in: Required Skills: Full-stack web development Mobile app development (iOS + Android) AI/LLM integrations Scalable backend architecture Cloud infrastructure UI/UX implementation API integrations Database architecture Preferred Tech Stack: React / Next.js Flutter or React Native Node.js / NestJS Python AI services OpenAI / Claude integrations AWS or GCP PostgreSQL Docker AI Features: The platform will include AI-powered capabilities such as: Conversational AI assistant AI-generated summaries Smart recommendations Workflow automation Semantic search / knowledge retrieval What We Need From the Agency: End-to-end development Strong communication Weekly progress updates Ability to scale team as needed Clean architecture and documentation Dedicated PM or technical lead To Apply: Please share: Relevant AI + SaaS projects Mobile apps you have built Team structure Estimated availability Suggested architecture approach Your preferred tech stack We are looking for a long-term collaboration with an agency capable of handling both MVP and scaling phases.', 1, 'HOURLY', 646000.00, 1214000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('6adf5149-d648-5e92-9e81-5e1b68952fa1', 'ed920451-6478-5c39-bf15-30cfcd6320c6', 'Full-Stack Developer (React, Node.js & Sui Move) — Existing Loyalty Rewards dApp', 'We run a live loyalty rewards dApp on the Sui blockchain, where small businesses issue digital loyalty points to customers for purchases. Our core Move smart contracts are already deployed and working. We’re looking for a mid-level or senior Full-Stack Developer with experience in React, Node.js, and Sui Move to help us improve and extend the existing platform. What You’ll Do - Update and extend existing Sui Move smart contracts with new loyalty rewards features. - Build and improve frontend interfaces using React and TypeScript. - Develop and maintain backend APIs and services using Node.js. - Integrate the React frontend and Node.js backend with existing Sui smart contracts. - Implement wallet connectivity, transaction signing, and on-chain transaction handling. - Fix minor bugs, improve application reliability, and expand automated test coverage. - Collaborate with the team to review the existing codebase and deliver incremental improvements. Required Experience - Solid experience with React, TypeScript, and modern frontend development. - Strong Node.js experience building APIs and backend services. - Practical experience with Sui Move and the Sui blockchain. - Experience integrating web applications with blockchain smart contracts. - Familiarity with Sui wallets, transaction execution, and the Sui TypeScript SDK. - Experience writing automated tests, debugging issues, and maintaining existing production applications. - Ability to work independently within an established codebase. Project Scope This is an ongoing development role focused on improving a working product. The core smart contracts are already deployed, and the platform is operational. We are not launching a new token, building an NFT marketplace, or developing protocol-level DeFi infrastructure. Our focus is on practical loyalty rewards functionality, full-stack integration, bug fixes, and code quality.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1033000.00, 2325000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a4c5e94d-f887-57bb-8e4d-a09d7a2be24b', 'a8034a6a-a36c-5302-ac00-52a50ca35fc9', 'Multi Agent Claude Debugging and Optimization for SaaS Application', 'We are looking for an experienced developer to debug and fix an existing multi agent AI system built with Claude for our SaaS application. The main challenges involve Python code errors, incorrect API requests, agent execution issues, and problems parsing AI generated responses. Agents are not consistently processing requests or returning the expected output, affecting the application''s functionality. The objective is to identify the root causes, fix the existing implementation, ensure requests are correctly constructed and processed, resolve response parsing issues, and improve the reliability of the overall agent workflow. Required Skills: Python, SQL, Claude API, multi agent AI workflows, JSON parsing, Microsoft Azure, and Databricks. Experience debugging existing AI applications and troubleshooting LLM API integrations is highly preferred.', 1, 'FIXED', 129000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e5318ceb-4901-5288-8476-5c4fbf35b762', '8235e02d-47a1-50b8-add7-17cd00543afb', 'Next.js + Supabase developer for creator link-in-bio startup', 'A year ago I started building a link-in-bio tool for creators, the kind where a musician or a coach gets one page that holds their links, a small shop, and a way for fans to send a tip. We''ve launched, a few hundred creators use it, and the money side is starting to matter. We''re a team of four, two of us technical, and we''re now looking for a developer to join long-term. The product is a Next.js app (App Router, TypeScript) on Vercel with Supabase behind it for database, auth and file storage. Payments run through Stripe Connect, so creators get paid straight to their own accounts. Most of the code is reasonably tidy, though some parts were written in a hurry and could use some love. Your days would be a mix of new features and fixing what users report. Right now on the list: a better analytics view for creators (clicks, tips, top links), custom domains for pages, email receipts after a tip, and some row level security cleanup in Supabase that has been sitting on the backlog for too long. Nothing exotic, but it needs someone who likes working directly with the product, not just tickets. We use GitHub with pull requests and review each other''s code, tasks live in Linear, and we do a short standup three times a week on video. Everyone talks to everyone, there''s no heavy process. You''d talk with me, the founder, about what to build and why, and with our other developer about how. We''re happy to take someone earlier in their career if they''re curious and write careful code. Tell us what you''ve built, even if it was a side project, and which part of it you''re most proud of.', 1, 'HOURLY', 517000.00, 542000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e7dbb0a1-45a9-55f1-afb9-cce4e20d3742', 'c2bc9324-fb3a-5b57-8110-aa62da441af4', 'Developer Needed to Build a Modern Football Club Management Web App for Makongi FC', 'Project Description: Makongi FC Football Club Management Web App I need a skilled web developer to build a modern, professional, and mobile-friendly football club management web app for Makongi FC. The platform should work online through a web browser without requiring users to download or install an app. Main Features Required: Player Management: Register players, add their names, jersey numbers, positions, and photos. Team Lineup: Create and display the starting XI, substitutes, formations, and player positions. Fixtures and Results: Publish upcoming matches, opponents, venues, kickoff times, and final scores. Player Statistics: Track goals, assists, appearances, and other player performance statistics. League Table: Display matches played, wins, draws, losses, goals, points, and standings. Matchday Posters: Create professional matchday and birthday posters for players. Club News: Publish announcements, match reports, and team updates. Admin Dashboard: Allow authorized administrators to manage players, matches, results, and club information. Club Branding: Use a modern red, black, and white design featuring the Makongi FC logo and the slogan “The Pride of Great Makongi FC.” Technical Requirements: Responsive design for Android phones, computers, and tablets. Secure login for administrators. Database to store player and match information. Easy-to-use interface with fast loading. Online hosting and a working website link. Complete source code and instructions for future maintenance. I am looking for a developer who can recommend a suitable technology, provide a clear budget and timeline, and deliver a fully functional product. Please include examples of similar projects you have completed, your estimated development cost, and the expected delivery time. Important: The first priority is a working web app that is accessible through a link. A native Android or iOS app can be considered in the future.', 1, 'HOURLY', 336000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00');

