    ('ab2680f3-ff6e-54e5-864c-4283e263ff5f', 'ebb7d566-8696-59ac-b86b-9a5b933966d5', 'Chỉnh sửa & phát triển website ASP.NET Web Forms', 'Mình đang cần tìm freelancer hoặc đội ngũ có kinh nghiệm với ASP.NET Web Forms / C# / SQL Server để tiếp nhận và phát triển một website doanh nghiệp đang vận hành. Website:...', 1, 'FIXED', 8000000.00, 10000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a3f41d17-9e95-5c2e-850f-5d360b6f610d', 'f437071f-4682-5ed8-a56a-af385f1720a9', 'Thuê người viết tool quét Following của X (Twitter) theo danh sách User chạy hàng loạt', 'Giá cả thỏa thuận. Mô tả nhu cầu: Tôi cần một phần mềm chạy trên Windows (đóng gói thành file .exe có giao diện bấm nút đơn giản, không chạy bằng dòng lệnh). Tính năng: Nạp một file targets.txt chứa danh sách các username cần quét. Phần mềm sẽ tự động cào danh sách Following của toàn bộ danh sách này cuốn chiếu từ trên xuống dưới và xuất ra 1 file Excel tổng hợp. Tôi mua 1 extension bản Pro quét rất mượt (quét vài triệu Followers vẫn ngon lành) nhưng chỉ có thể quét từng user. Bạn có thể dựa vào SOURCE CODE GỐC của một extension Chrome (bản PRO chạy rất mượt, cào được số lượng lớn không bị chặn) để viết theo cho nhanh.', 1, 'FIXED', 200000.00, 100000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('ef56f88b-2125-5569-a674-b260632482cf', '0e759c91-9f3d-57db-a5c1-5bcf969946a8', 'Cần hỗ trợ nâng cấp thêm chữ ký số vào phần mềm', 'Mình có ứng dụng chay trên nền tảng php và js hiên tại cần xư lý bổ sung chữ ký số và bệnh án điện tử, trên vlance có bán nào đã làm liên hệ với mình nhé', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 2000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('88845dae-e3d5-5ac2-83a0-61c502a57126', '642e42c5-9bde-560d-a505-f20fb6e8ccb9', 'Thiết kế mọi trang web theo yêu cầu', 'Thiết kế và lập trình giao diện (Frontend): Xây dựng các trang chính gồm Trang chủ, Trang danh mục, Chi tiết, Giỏ hàng, Thanh toán và Trang quản trị (nếu có). Giao diện cần chuẩn Responsive trên mọi thiết bị', 1, 'FIXED', 500000.00, 15000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b7bf8ed3-c832-5022-bbe8-7438c9db2d62', '15731531-93e9-5f29-b0c4-3e8647d03732', 'Website for Solo Practice Law Firm', 'I need a professional website for my solo practice law firm. The site should present my services clearly, include a strong attorney profile, and provide a reliable way for clients to contact me. I’m looking for someone who can create a polished, trustworthy online presence that reflects my practice and makes it easy for potential clients to reach out.', 1, 'FIXED', 6458000.00, 6458000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('8cd0af86-b5d2-5b69-81a6-2fe47ebbc2e8', 'a6c15798-a8cc-5547-9754-d54d382b1afd', 'Restaurant Website Development', 'Create a modern, responsive website with a premium design, smooth animations, a clean user interface, and mobile-friendly layout. Make it simple, attractive, and easy to use.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4ce8a19d-b4b9-55bd-b719-556f9a99df3a', 'ee807b43-939a-5fd6-badd-c2ff246642e3', 'QA Tester Needed for a B2B Agentic AI Startup - Extremely fast paced environment', 'QA Engineer/Tester for Agentic AI Products (Very Fast-Paced, Independent Role) Project Details Seeking a sharp & fast QA tester to deeply test our AI Agentic SaaS platform on web and mobile. Your mission: uncover maximum bugs, crashes, and UX breakers to strengthen the product. Must handle high expectations and deliver fast, structured results. Key Tasks: -Conduct exhaustive manual testing: functional, usability, edge cases, and exploratory on web/mobile. - Prioritize critical issues impacting users (e.g., breaks, crashes). - Log everything with reproducible steps, screenshots/videos, severity ratings. - Design/execute test plans: functional, regression, smoke, exploratory, usability for AI behaviors/decision chains. - Validate multi-step flows, logic gaps, guardrails, edge cases, cascading failures. - Build synthetic scripts for UI, APIs, E2E flows; test web/mobile/integrations. - Maintain dashboards for coverage, failures, KPIs; partner with Prod/Design/Eng on requirements/go-no-go. - Optimize tests: fix flakiness, parallel runs, reduce time; monitor pre/post-release quality to refine AI evals. Must-Haves: -QA experience with SaaS/web/mobile apps. -Proven bug-hunting skills (share examples/portfolio). -Detail-focused, quick turnaround, excellent English communication. Deliverables: -Detailed bug report spreadsheet (issue, steps, impact, priority). -Summary of high-impact findings. -Test coverage summary. ​', 1, 'HOURLY', 103000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0c4e1258-2b7d-5a42-b97b-f39461e64195', 'b78c97d7-0f90-5918-a2a1-3f63c719247a', 'AI Agent Development and Training', 'I am seeking an experienced freelancer to help build an AI agent tailored to my needs and provide guidance on the process. The ideal candidate will create the AI solution and also explain the underlying principles and techniques for my understanding. This project aims to empower me with practical skills in AI development and implementation. If you have expertise in AI technologies and a passion for teaching, I would love to collaborate with you.', 1, 'HOURLY', 77000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('92ddbdc8-8f2f-5a9d-8370-66ca658de673', '97f2e56a-d24b-58a5-a06d-ba12c43a9c61', 'AI Agent Developer Needed', 'I’m looking for an AI Agent Developer to build a simple AI agent using tools like OpenAI API, Python, LangChain, or n8n. Requirements: Experience with AI agents and LLMs API integration and automation Good communication skills Please share your relevant experience and previous projects.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1550000.00, 3100000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('259bf782-ce6b-5921-9fe6-ee1c7e02b0ea', '97f2e56a-d24b-58a5-a06d-ba12c43a9c61', 'AI Agent Creator and QA/Tester (Claude, Gumloop, N8N, CrewAI, UiPath, OpenClaw)', '⚠️ DO NOT CONTACT OUTSIDE OF UPWORK! DO NOT EMAIL OUTSIDE OF UPWORK! FOLLOW INSTRUCTIONS!⚠️ NDA SIGNING REQUIRED FOR HIRED CANDIDATE! YOU MUST PROVIDE REGULAR REPORTING AND STATUS UPDATES. ## AI Agent Builder & API Tester We are looking for an experienced **AI Agent Builder & Tester** to help test an AI Agent Action Security platform. Your role will be to create, configure, and operate AI agents across leading agent platforms, then integrate those agents with the **Enterprise API** to test real-world action scenarios. Platforms and technologies may include: - Claude - Google Gemini Enterprise - Microsoft Copilot Studio - Salesforce Agentforce - ServiceNow Now Assist / AI Agents - Shopify - GitHub - LangStack.com - Gumloop - n8n - CrewAI - UiPath - OpenClaw - Hermes - Meta/Facebook AI tools - Grok - Other major AI-agent platforms You should be comfortable building agent workflows, making API calls, working with JSON, webhooks, authentication, and troubleshooting integrations. Testing will include both routine and high-impact AI-agent actions involving areas such as CRM data, commerce, repositories, permissions, data exports, financial actions, and enterprise workflows. **You are expected to have your own access to the platforms being tested**, using existing paid accounts, developer accounts, or available trials. We will provide approved **Enterprise Sandbox access**, API documentation, testing scenarios, and technical guidance. Please include examples of AI agents or agent workflows you have previously built and the platforms you have experience with. First questions/interview will be done via Upwork messages. Next we will have brief zoom call interview. Selected candidate will be chosen within 1-week.', 1, 'HOURLY', 77000.00, 103000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f9f21150-07f3-5680-8e4b-f35670bca04f', '97f2e56a-d24b-58a5-a06d-ba12c43a9c61', 'AI Agent Integration – n8n and LLM Agent for Lead Qualification and CRM Updates', 'We need a freelancer to build an automated workflow that connects n8n with a CRM and an LLM agent for lead qualification. The project includes setting up the workflow, integrating the CRM, connecting the LLM agent, and testing the full process. You will also document the setup and provide guidance for future maintenance. The ideal freelancer should be comfortable working with automation tools and AI agents to create a reliable lead qualification system.', 1, 'FIXED', 517000.00, 517000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('86f9d045-f494-5cf0-b165-03443f330511', '1b31ccb1-1f75-57f0-ad17-d5025d93f12c', 'USA ONLY Full-Stack Developer — Next.js, Technical SEO & Agentic Development Tools', 'Overview: We are a growth operations company that builds the digital infrastructure behind agencies and their clients. We rebuild websites, develop custom software applications, and deploy technical SEO and attribution systems that directly drive client revenue. We work fast, we work lean, and we use modern agentic development tools to deliver in weeks what used to take months. We are looking for a full-stack developer to join us on an hourly contract basis with the strong potential for a long-term ongoing relationship as we scale. This is not a traditional development role. You will be expected to use Claude Code, Cursor, or comparable AI-assisted development tools as a core part of your workflow — not as an occasional helper but as your primary development accelerator. If you are not already building this way, this is not the right role for you. What You Will Be Working On: Our clients are real businesses — law firms, industrial companies, agencies — who need their digital infrastructure rebuilt correctly and maintained consistently. Here is the kind of work you will own: Website builds on Next.js with a headless CMS, hosted on Vercel. You will take clients from outdated legacy platforms like WordPress, Concrete5, or Webflow to fully modern production sites. Typical delivery window is two to three weeks per site. Technical SEO infrastructure including 301 redirect mapping from legacy URLs, sitemap generation, Google Search Console setup, Schema markup implementation throughout the site covering Organization, Product, Service, Attorney, LegalService, and FAQ structured data, and ongoing monthly crawl monitoring and remediation. Custom software application development including interactive web tools, lead qualification utilities, case value calculators, legal process visualizers, and intake automation systems. These are client-facing applications that need to perform reliably and integrate cleanly with CRMs and third-party systems. Revenue attribution dashboard configuration pulling from Google Analytics GA4, active traffic channels, and client CRM pipelines including Dynamics 365 and HubSpot. API integrations connecting rebuilt websites and custom applications to existing client systems. You will not always be rebuilding these systems — you will often be connecting to them, auditing them, and extending them. Database architecture using Supabase where client engagements require data storage for custom applications, lead tracking, or interactive tools. Ongoing monthly development support across multiple active client engagements covering new page builds, feature iterations, bug fixes, Schema markup updates, and application improvements. What We Need From You: Strong proficiency in Next.js, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind. You should be able to scaffold and deploy a production Next.js application with a headless CMS, proper SEO infrastructure, and Supabase database connectivity without needing guidance. Hands-on daily experience with Claude Code, Cursor, or a comparable agentic development tool. We will ask you about your specific workflow in screening. Candidates who cannot describe a concrete agentic development workflow will not move forward. Working knowledge of technical SEO. Not surface level. You should understand how crawlers work, what Schema markup does and how to implement it correctly, why 301 redirects matter for domain authority, and how Core Web Vitals scores affect search rankings. API integration experience. Most of our client engagements involve connecting a new website or application to an existing system. You need to be comfortable reading API documentation and building reliable integrations independently. GA4 configuration and event tracking setup. You need to be able to wire up tracking correctly and know when it is broken. Experience managing multiple concurrent projects. You will have two to four active client engagements running simultaneously at different stages of the delivery cycle. Strong written communication in English. You will not be client-facing directly but you will be submitting deliverables, writing documentation, and flagging issues clearly and quickly. Communication speed and clarity matters as much as technical skill in this role. Project management and a strong understanding of the code review and security process for application development are critical. You may also be client facing.', 1, 'HOURLY', 775000.00, 1808000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('08faa9c7-92c5-5f35-b61e-50ebc85ee36e', '2db0b304-6c80-5745-904e-3d737f23263d', 'AI Chatbot Developer Needed – RAG-Based Customer Support Assistant (OpenAI/Claude + Next.js)', 'We’re a mid-sized e-commerce company with about 2,000 support tickets a month. Most are repetitive questions about orders, returns, and product details. We want an AI assistant that answers these automatically using our own knowledge base, and hands off to a human agent when it can’t. What we need: A chatbot widget embedded on our Next.js website Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) over our help docs, FAQs and product catalog (around 500 pages) Integration with our order system through a REST API, so the bot can check order status Human handoff to our Freshdesk account when confidence is low A simple admin panel to upload or update knowledge base documents Basic analytics: questions asked, resolution rate, handoff rate Tech preferences: LLM: OpenAI or Claude (open to your recommendation) Vector DB: Pinecone, Supabase pgvector or similar Backend: Node.js or Python Deliverables: Working chatbot deployed on our staging site Source code in our GitHub repo Documentation for updating the knowledge base Two weeks of post-launch support Ideal freelancer: Has built and shipped at least two RAG or LLM-based applications Understands prompt engineering, hallucination control and evaluation Communicates clearly and gives regular progress updates To apply, please answer: Share a link or demo of an AI chatbot or RAG system you’ve built. How would you prevent the bot from giving incorrect answers about our policies? Which LLM and vector database would you recommend for this, and why? What’s your estimated timeline?', 1, 'HOURLY', 491000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('886d0edd-07eb-5c59-b586-682802678806', '2db0b304-6c80-5745-904e-3d737f23263d', 'OpenAI API & LangChain Expert to Fix a Broken RAG Chatbot', 'We built a custom chatbot using Python, LangChain, and Pinecone to answer queries based on our company wiki. Unfortunately, the current implementation has several issues. The chatbot sometimes hallucinates, provides incorrect or overly generic answers, and occasionally crashes. The chunking strategy may need improvement, and the prompts may need to be rewritten. We’re looking for an experienced developer to audit the existing code, fix the RAG pipeline, improve retrieval accuracy, and make the chatbot reliable. The goal is to ensure the chatbot provides accurate, relevant answers based on our company knowledge base. To Apply: Please describe your experience with OpenAI API, LangChain, Pinecone, and debugging RAG systems. Share relevant examples of similar projects you’ve worked on.', 1, 'FIXED', 2583000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('3f27f554-60fc-5847-b359-f77b4997166d', '5e6d8852-ccca-5937-88eb-1d59fa8198d6', 'WordPress Site for Business Brokerage (WA Cannabis I-502, Bilingual + AI Chatbot)', 'We are a Washington State licensed cannabis (I-502) business brokerage. We need an experienced WordPress developer to build a clean, professional, bilingual (English + Chinese) website that showcases cannabis businesses for sale and generates qualified buyer and seller leads. Reference site for style and functionality: https://www.green-rush.us SCOPE / DELIVERABLES 1. Domain and hosting setup (help choose/configure hosting, SSL, email-ready DNS). 2. Pages: Home, About, Services, Available Listings, Sell Your Business, Buyer Intake, Contact. 3. Listings directory: searchable and filterable (e.g., license type, location/county, price range, status), with an easy admin workflow so the owner can add, edit, and mark listings sold without a developer. 4. Forms: "Sell Your Business" intake form and Buyer intake form (with confidentiality/NDA acknowledgment), plus a general contact form; submissions emailed to the owner and stored in WordPress. 5. AI chatbot: answers common questions (process, fees, licensing basics, how to buy/sell) and captures buyer/seller lead details into the same lead inbox. 6. Bilingual English/Chinese with a language toggle on every page (owner will review/provide translations as needed). 7. Fully mobile responsive and fast-loading. 8. Basic on-page SEO (titles, meta, schema, sitemap), plus Google Business Profile and Google Search Console setup. 9. Owner training and handoff: a short walkthrough session/video and simple written guide for adding listings and managing leads; all admin logins transferred to the owner. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (definition of done) - All listed pages live on the owner''s domain with SSL, in both English and Chinese. - Owner can add a new listing in under 10 minutes and it appears in search/filter results. - Every form and the chatbot deliver a test lead to the owner''s email and the WordPress admin. - Site passes Google''s mobile-friendly check and loads well on mobile. - Sitemap submitted in Google Search Console; Google Business Profile set up. - Training delivered and documentation handed over. Budget: up to $5,000 (maximum). Please quote your own fixed price for the full scope; competitive quotes below the cap are welcome. Milestones welcome. TO APPLY, please include: - Links to relevant portfolio work, especially cannabis-industry and/or business brokerage or listings sites. - Your proposed timeline with milestones. - Your fixed-price quote for the full scope above.', 1, 'FIXED', 129160000.00, 129160000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('38713418-bb71-573b-be2e-cd2e4394fb6a', '2b63c471-0e5b-5db7-bbed-c6d2e58de3f1', 'Wanted: Dev to join team Building Agentic Guardail System', 'Wanted: Dev who knows python, C/C++ and has experience turning Linux programs into MacOS. we need a real dev to come in and make sure the architecture is sound. Ideally you like architecture and routing systems, you can help us take it from a Linux program to be macOS ready. You should be strong in: C/C++ and Python Cross-platform porting, Linux → macOS (Apple Silicon) Build systems (CMake), macOS code signing + notarization Starting ASAP, work for hire, NDA required, lots of hours now, kinda a one time job. After we do mac, we'' want to get it operational for windows. codbase is largely finished in Linux now. Bonus points if you have any experience with audio engineering. Thanks, Team Primedian C++ macOS port, cross-platform C++, Apple Silicon, code signing notarization, CMake, Linux macOS porting. Judgment on someone else’s finished code — reading an unfamiliar codebase, deciding what’s sound and what breaks on a new platform. Needed. Cross-platform porting — knowing where Linux and macOS diverge (filesystem, process model, linking, signals) before it bites you. Needed. The Python↔C/C++ boundary holding up across platforms.', 1, 'HOURLY', 491000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('2d209dd0-1800-5b95-99fb-69f645e6d88a', '241e4f48-83bb-533e-b12e-62b967bd2d2c', 'DevOps Expert with AI/LLM/RAG/Agentic experience', 'We’re seeking a DevOps expert with strong AI, RAG, LLM, and agentic experience and a focus on data privacy to support consulting work and potentially join our team as a fractional CTO. This role will help shape our technical direction, improve infrastructure, and guide AI-driven initiatives. We’d love to schedule a short chat to discuss the opportunity and see if it aligns with your expertise and interests. Please note this is a HANDS-ON job not just a strategy position. Along with a junior team you will scope, plan, develop and ship.', 1, 'HOURLY', 646000.00, 1162000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a7d678f4-be39-55c6-97a4-b64f0bd13155', '241e4f48-83bb-533e-b12e-62b967bd2d2c', 'AI Engineer & Data Engineer Needed | LLM, RAG, LangChain, AI Agents & Power BI', 'We are looking for a skilled and experienced AI Engineer / Data Engineer to join our team and help us develop intelligent AI solutions and data-driven applications. The ideal freelancer should have strong knowledge of Generative AI, Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), LangChain, AI Agents, Data Engineering, ETL pipelines, Data Visualization, and Microsoft Power BI. The candidate should be capable of developing LLM-powered applications, building RAG-based systems for document search and question answering, creating AI agents to automate tasks and workflows, and integrating AI models with external data sources and APIs. We are also looking for expertise in designing and maintaining ETL pipelines, data extraction, cleaning, transformation, and integration, as well as preparing data for AI applications and analytics. Experience in developing interactive Power BI dashboards, creating meaningful data visualizations, and transforming complex datasets into actionable business insights is highly desirable. The ideal freelancer should have practical experience with Python, APIs, databases, vector databases, embeddings, and AI frameworks, along with strong problem-solving skills and the ability to recommend suitable technical solutions based on project requirements. We value clear communication, attention to detail, clean and maintainable code, and the ability to work independently while meeting agreed deadlines. Please share relevant portfolio projects, your experience with these technologies, your availability, and your hourly or project-based rate when applying.', 1, 'HOURLY', 465000.00, 1085000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('5d1c7827-1166-50fa-bfd8-974184d022f6', '6035dbba-ef7a-51b4-a14e-97e24288948d', 'Python/FastAPI + LangGraph engineer to take an LLM product to beta launch', 'I''m a founder building an early-stage software product that uses LLMs to help professional services teams with complex written work. The backend is built and has been through an independent security review. I''m now looking for an engineer to take it through hardening, deployment and an invite-only beta. THE STACK Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, PostgreSQL with pgvector, Alembic, Django (admin), S3-compatible object storage, Anthropic and OpenAI APIs, LangSmith. WHAT''S NEXT - Security hardening from the review: rate limiting, auth and tokens, tenant isolation - Updating the model integration to newer LLM versions and managing cost per run - Production deployment to the cloud - Connecting the front end for beta users - Ongoing features after launch WHAT I''M LOOKING FOR - 2–5 years building production backends in Python - Hands-on experience shipping LLM apps: agent workflows, RAG, prompt and cost management - Solid understanding of multi-tenant data security - Clear written communication. You''ll be working with a non-technical founder, so explaining trade-offs plainly matters. - Nice to have: cloud deployment (AWS, GCP or similar), React, Stripe HOW IT WORKS - Ongoing hourly contract, around 15–25 hours a week to start - Some overlap with Australian business hours (AEST) - A senior engineer reviews architecture and security - Starts with a short paid trial task - NDA and IP assignment required before access to the codebase Independent freelancers only, please, no agencies. To show you''ve read this, start your proposal with the word "pgvector".', 1, 'HOURLY', 517000.00, 904000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('d54ad1cd-df09-5d49-a2ce-544925a03d42', '8f1d8b42-fb15-5aa1-9dfb-d824498e4c02', 'AI Developer – LangGraph Agents & LLM Fine-Tuning', 'I''m looking for an experienced AI developer to help build production-grade agentic AI systems using LangGraph and to fine-tune LLMs for domain-specific tasks. This is hands-on development work with potential for a long-term engagement. What you''ll do: - Design and build multi-agent workflows in LangGraph (state graphs, tool calling, memory, human-in-the-loop, conditional routing) - Integrate agents with APIs, databases and vector stores (RAG pipelines) - Fine-tune open-source LLMs (Llama, Mistral, Qwen, etc.) using LoRA/QLoRA, PEFT or full fine-tuning - Prepare and clean training datasets, run evaluations and benchmark against base models - Deploy and serve models (vLLM, TGI, Hugging Face, or cloud GPUs such as AWS/GCP/RunPod) - Set up observability and evaluation (LangSmith, Langfuse or similar) - Write clean, documented Python code and give clear progress updates Requirements: - Proven experience with LangGraph and LangChain in real projects (please share links or examples) - Hands-on LLM fine-tuning experience (Hugging Face Transformers, PEFT, TRL, Unsloth) - Strong Python skills; FastAPI is a plus - Experience with OpenAI, Anthropic or open-source model APIs - Solid understanding of prompt engineering, RAG and evaluation methods - Good communication and ability to work independently Nice to have: - Experience with DPO / RLHF - Docker and CI/CD for ML deployment - Experience with voice AI or SaaS products To apply, please include: 1. A short summary of a LangGraph project you''ve built 2. A fine-tuning project you''ve done (model, method, results) 3. Your availability and hourly rate Proposals starting with "Dear Sir/Madam" or generic templates will be skipped.', 1, 'HOURLY', 775000.00, 1550000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00');

