    updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at; document the recommended approach and any limitations. - Make attribution gaps visible rather than presenting uncertain data as definitive. - Deliver usable reporting - Build a live dashboard for daily, weekly, and monthly traffic and funnel performance, with filters for website, blog, Unbounce landing pages, campaign, source/medium, device, language, and new/returning audience where available. - Show traffic volume alongside CTA clicks, CTA submissions, and subsequent qualified leads or orders. - Report funnel conversion and drop-off by page and journey—for example, landing page → CTA click → form or order submission—and highlight where tracking is incomplete. - Make reports practical for Product and Marketing to use together, rather than creating another disconnected dashboard. Nice To Have: Support SEO and website improvement Review technical SEO and organic search performance, including indexability, site structure, page speed, internal linking, and relevant Search Console data. Separate branded and non-branded organic performance, and distinguish storage-intent content from broader informational blog traffic where feasible. Recommend a prioritized set of SEO and conversion improvements, with expected measurement and success criteria. KPI scope Reporting should align with Spacebox’s Product KPI definitions, including qualified organic and paid sessions; including but not limited to: web channel impressions and click-through-rates qualified visit → lead; qualified visit → order start; order start → submission; CTA conversion by journey; Blog → commercial-page progression; and downstream lead or order outcomes. Where available, connect these to activated customers and activated MRR—not just traffic or form submissions. Definitions should specify the cohort, denominator, exclusions, source of truth, cadence, and trust level. Deliverables - Current-state audit — data sources, tracking gaps, reconciliation issues, exclusions, and