    updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at; preparation of new legal policies or legal advice is not included unless separately approved. MLS Integration Include the custom OBAR / Paragon OpenMLS integration and automated Home Valuation integration described in this SOW. Third-party service subscriptions, licensing, hosting, MLS access, and API usage fees are paid directly by Erica Arnold. Deliver property search with town, price, beds, baths, property type, waterfront, and sorting filters, together with commercial categories supported by the authorized API. Provide website-native property detail pages with galleries and property-specific showing or information requests. Route Contact, Sell, Home Value, property-specific, and applicable commercial inquiries securely to my email address with server-side processing, validation, spam protection, error handling, verified delivery, and clear success or failure states. Include relevant form details and property identifiers or URLs, and send Erica copies of automated confirmation messages delivered to users; confirm the sender address and transactional email provider before implementation.', 1, 'FIXED', 38748000.00, 38748000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0f00b8b1-bd4f-5854-b1fd-2883c3d1d817', '63ec306b-d1d0-5053-b3fc-78bebc436f42', 'Responsive Real Estate webiste Design (Rent & Sale)', 'PROJECT PROPOSAL Luxury Property Experience Platform in the Dominican Republic PROJECT OVERVIEW This platform is much more than a conventional real estate website. Its success depends on delivering: • A luxury browsing experience • Airbnb-inspired search and filtering • Fast property discovery • Mobile responsiveness across all devices • A presentation that inspires trust • Organized property management to ensure scalability The platform will showcase the complete portfolio of luxury properties available for rent and sale. It will also promote concierge-style services, including: • Grocery shopping • Airport transfers • Villa staff training • Equipment rentals • Boat Rentals • Car Rentals • Shuttles • Chefs • Cribs • Car Seats The experience should feel modern, elegant, fast, and intuitive. BUSINESS AND USER EXPERIENCE OBJECTIVES • Luxury Property Presentation o Showcase premium properties through elegant layouts, high-quality imagery, and organized content. • Airbnb-Inspired Browsing Experience o Enable visitors to find properties easily through intuitive search and filters. • Inquiry Generation o Encourage qualified inquiries via WhatsApp, phone, and email. • Scalability o Create a structured backend that supports future expansion and property management. • Multilingual Accessibility o Support English and Spanish. • Mobile-First Experience o Ensure optimal performance on desktop computers, tablets, and mobile devices. PLATFORM APPROACH Content Management System (CMS) and Architecture • WordPress CMS • Custom content types for properties • Structured database architecture • Advanced filtering system • Scalable content management Key Integrations • Google Maps API • WhatsApp integration • SEO optimization • Secure authentication • Spam protection • Multilingual support (English and Spanish) UX/UI Direction • Airbnb-inspired navigation flow • Caribbean luxury-inspired presentation • Clean, responsive layouts • Seamless interactions • Optimized mobile experience • Fast-loading image galleries This approach ensures scalability, easy content management, a strong SEO foundation, and flexibility for future growth. DEVELOPMENT APPROACH The project should follow a structured, milestone-based process, with review and approval checkpoints at each major phase. • Validating user experience (UX) before development begins. • Organized execution phases. • Continuous feedback integration. • Predictable delivery structure. • Scalable architecture planning. • Quality assurance (QA) before deployment. This approach helps reduce the risk of revisions, improve communication, and maintain project quality. WORK PROCESS • Weekly progress updates. • Milestone-based reviews. • Clearly defined approval checkpoints. • Integration of comments and feedback at each phase. • Testing and quality assurance (QA) before launch. • Organized delivery structure. • Ongoing communication throughout project execution. The goal is to maintain visibility, predictability, and alignment among all parties throughout project development. KEY FEATURES Property Listings Each property will include: • Detailed description property card • High-resolution image galleries • Amenities and features • Property rules • Cancellation policies • Google Maps integration • WhatsApp, email, and phone contact options • User comments and reviews • Calendar for tentative reservation date selection Airbnb-Inspired Search and Filtering Filters will include: • Destination • Property type • Number of bedrooms • Number of bathrooms • Number of Guests • Number of beds Special attention will be given to maintaining an intuitive, mobile-optimized experience. USER FEATURES Users need to be able to: • Register and log in • Save favorite properties • Post comments and reviews The system will include login pop-up safeguards to prevent content loss when posting comments. It is preferable to first allow the user to write the review and when they click submit, it should redirect to user creation and login page and once completed, the review is posted. PROPERTY SUBMISSIONS BY OWNERS Property owners will be able to submit requests through: “Add Your Property / List Your Villa” The process will include: • Submission of property information (location, contact number) • Image uploads • Automatic administrator notifications • Manual review and approval No property should be published automatically. PERFORMANCE, SEO, AND RESPONSIVENESS Special attention to: • Speed optimization • Mobile responsiveness • Search engine optimization (SEO)-friendly structure • Structured metadata • Image optimization • Responsive layouts • Cross-device compatibility • Search and filter optimization The Booking option will require a short form to be completed prior to sending the message that includes: o Start and end dates o Amount of People o Amount of Rooms o E-mail and WhatsApp number PROJECT DELIVERY PLAN AND MILESTONES MILESTONE I User Experience (UX) / User Interface (UI) Strategy, Luxury Experience, and Design Approval Deliverables:  Brand-aligned design  Information architecture  Homepage design  Rental and sales page designs  Property detail page design  Airbnb-inspired search experience  Concierge page designs  Contact page design  Responsive designs for mobile and tablet  Design revisions MILESTONE II Development of a Scalable Property Platform. Includes:  Property catalog  Rental listings  Sales listings  Detail pages  Amenities and features  Cancellation policies  Google Maps integration  WhatsApp, email, and phone  CMS configuration  Responsive implementation MILESTONE III Optimization, User Experience, and Launch Preparation Includes:  Registration and login  Favorites  Comments and reviews system  Review history  “Add Your Property” form  SEO optimization  Mobile optimization  English and Spanish configuration  Full QA  Deployment and launch POST-LAUNCH SUPPORT 30 day support:  Bug fixes  Minor adjustments  Launch monitoring  Technical assistance TERMS AND CONSIDERATIONS The proposal assumes that: • The client will provide content, branding, and property information. CONCLUSION This project has significant potential to become a leading luxury real estate platform in the Dominican Republic for travelers, renters, buyers, and property owners. Success will depend on balancing: • Luxury presentation • Browsing speed • Mobile responsiveness • Organized property discovery • Scalable architecture • Intuitive user experience The proposed structure must be designed to minimize risks, maintain high quality standards, and deliver a premium experience aligned with the luxury real estate market. The website should be design taking https://www.argentoba.com as a benchmark. This site is clean and easy to navigate. NOTE: This is a guide for the proposal. Feel free to improve the proposal wherever you may see suited.', 1, 'FIXED', 30998000.00, 30998000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a9609b2d-ab20-5225-8d98-a68d6778f597', '63ec306b-d1d0-5053-b3fc-78bebc436f42', 'Real Estate IDX Website Expert | IDX Optimization', 'The client needed a minor optimization on their real estate IDX website. Some property listing details were not displaying as expected, and the listing layout needed a quick review. The goal was to improve the property browsing experience while keeping the existing website design intact.', 1, 'FIXED', 129000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('284d9beb-c568-51bf-b3ca-eef3bdefd5f6', '829954a8-e8f9-57e2-81fc-2f8bf65fbc60', 'Full Stack Dev or Small Team to Build Well-Defined Real Estate Work Order Platform', 'You: A full-stack developer (or small team) who wants to help a smaller business build a new operational tool, with the opportunity to develop a longer-term relationship for future support and enhancements. You should be comfortable using AI assistance for routine development while applying your own developer expertise to document, secure, test, and manage the process. Us: A small Northeastern U.S. commercial real estate company looking to transition away from a COTS product for its maintenance team in favor of something that fits our needs substantially better. What: We are looking to replace a CMMS (incumbent details will be shared with shortlisted bidders) that no longer meets our needs and creates too much friction within our core operations. We are not starting from a blank page. We have a functional specification, logical ERD, accounting/export specification, Figma direction, UI guidelines, successful legacy CSV examples, and a proposed technology direction ready for developer review. How: We’ve identified a number of well-established open-source libraries that we believe can be leveraged to accelerate development within the broader functional brief, including Mantine and TanStack, with initial deployment contemplated through Supabase and Vercel. Goal: The goal is a milestone-based, production-ready V1 with strong direction and intentional scope delineation to prevent scope creep. Separately, we would also like a proposal for a one-year support arrangement after handoff that gives everyone clear expectations and helps ensure the effort remains successful. While nothing is certain at this point, if the initial effort is successful and we validate the related operational changes internally, there is a strong possibility of a V2 with several enhancements. Where possible, we prefer to continue working with people with whom we have built a successful relationship. This is not a “make me a cool app” or “bootstrap startup building an MVP for VC investment” project. We are an established small business with defined workflows seeking a tool that helps us operate better, including a PWA for field work. The current V1 schema is approximately 40–50 tables, but the model is built around straightforward relationships such as Site → Building → Location; Entity → Lease → Location; Work Order → Labor / Parts / Assets; and Scheduled Maintenance Plan → Occurrence → Work Order. The table count grows largely because we preserve history and normalize many-to-many relationships rather than embedding excessive complexity into individual records. The documentation is detailed because we have intentionally worked through business rules, edge cases, permissions, and accounting behavior before development begins. Given that, we believe this project is best suited for a single developer or small team working directly with us. We want the developer to challenge technical assumptions where appropriate, but we do not expect a substantial discovery phase to redefine the underlying workflows.', 1, 'FIXED', 258320000.00, 258320000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4b93b509-6b9c-532f-980c-f7116be7b592', '24d857b7-c943-5ccd-91c6-41f5a4d3ce17', 'Security review of a Lovable / Supabase web app (real estate CRM)', 'I''m a Realtor who built a real estate CRM called Firme for my brokerage team using Lovable, on Lovable Cloud (Supabase: Postgres, row-level security, edge functions, storage, scheduled jobs). It is live and used by 5 agents. It holds client names, emails, phone numbers, birthdays and deal information, so I want an independent security review before we grow. What I need: - Review of row-level security policies on all tables: can one agent see or change another agent''s data? - Review of storage buckets: who can list, read or upload files (listing photos, client home photos, documents). - Review of edge functions and database functions (including SECURITY DEFINER functions): can a signed-in user, or someone not signed in, use them to read data or send email or texts they should not? - Review of public pages: client intake forms and home evaluation forms, which anyone with a link can submit. - Review of the invite and sign-in flow. - Review of the sending paths: email blasts and campaigns (Brevo), connected Outlook mailboxes (Microsoft OAuth) and texting (Twilio). How it works: - Read-only access to the GitHub repository. - A Practice account with invented data for any testing. No access to real client data, and no changes to the live site or database. - An automated scan has already flagged several issues. I will share that report after hire, under NDA. Deliverable: - A written report, ranked by severity, with: what the issue is, who could exploit it (anyone, any signed-in user, a specific role), what data or action is exposed, how you confirmed it, and the smallest recommended fix. - Clear notes on anything the automated scan flagged that is NOT a real issue. - A 30-minute call to walk me through it. I am not a developer, so plain language matters. Fixes are not part of this job. My builder will make them, and I may hire you later to review the fixes. I''m open to a phased quote: Phase 1 covering row-level security, storage and public pages, and Phase 2 covering the sending paths. If you quote in phases, please price each one separately. Please include in your proposal: - Your experience with Supabase row-level security and storage policies specifically. - One example of a similar review you''ve done (no client details needed). - Your fixed price and timeline. NDA required before access.', 1, 'FIXED', 38748000.00, 38748000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('2b400466-aabb-5b3a-85d0-40feac76d051', '39747884-5ec5-55da-aec9-626b090422a3', 'Senior Python / AI Engineer to build AI platform for real estate agencies (RAG, API integrations)', 'I''m building an AI-powered SaaS platform for real estate agencies, starting with the UAE market. The goal is to cut the manual work agents do every day with developer brochures, payment plans, listings and leads. Full requirements are in the attached PDF. Please read it before applying. What the platform does: • Turns unstructured developer documents (PDF brochures, payment plans, floor plans, price lists) into a structured, searchable property database • Lets agents search, filter and compare projects and units with exact, source-backed data (price, size, payment plan, handover date, service charges) • Generates client-ready materials: unit comparisons, offer summaries, follow-up messages in English and Arabic • Qualifies incoming leads and matches them to suitable units • Syncs with CRMs and listing portals via API • Offers an AI assistant for agents and an embeddable widget for agency websites MVP scope: • Multi-tenant backend on FastAPI + PostgreSQL • Document ingestion and structured data extraction from messy PDFs and tables • Hybrid search: structured filters + vector search (pgvector or Qdrant, your recommendation) • LLM layer with RAG, source citations and strict validation for prices and numbers • REST API for integrations, first CRM connector • Eval set to measure extraction and answer accuracy • Docker, CI/CD, AWS deploy Requirements: • 5+ years Python in production • At least one shipped LLM/RAG product with real users • Strong experience with PDF and table data extraction • API integrations with third-party systems (CRM, webhooks) • You make architecture decisions and explain trade-offs • React/Next.js for a simple admin panel is a strong plus • 3-4 hours overlap with GST Process: paid test task (4-6 hours), then MVP in ~6-8 weeks, then long-term work if we''re a good fit. How to apply: • Start your proposal with "payment plan" • Answer: how would you make sure the platform never shows a wrong price or payment plan? • Send a rough estimate for the MVP scope from the attached PDF: hours per main block (ingestion and extraction, search, LLM layer, API and CRM connector, deploy) and the total • Record a short Loom (2-5 minutes): introduce yourself and walk through one LLM/RAG project you built - the architecture, the main problem you solved and what you would do differently today Proposals without a Loom and an estimate will not be reviewed.', 1, 'HOURLY', 904000.00, 1808000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('cfa93ba6-fde9-53d7-84b7-0cb48d8c1323', 'aede74ea-ed24-5048-ac55-b5a09f59a4ed', 'Create a Website for an Investment Firm', 'The job is to create a Website for a new Investment Firm. The website will be 1 landing page and 1-3 subpages. It shall not look like AI. Please only respond if you have done projects for Private Equity, Venture Capital, Real Estate, Consulting Businesses and have an understanding of designs in the industry.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1292000.00, 3875000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('bda4fbbe-2d26-5300-a917-ef7a3a05d0c3', '2869bc81-587d-5497-bbc8-84641d0caa72', 'Website Repositioning Specialist', 'We’re looking for an experienced Investor Carrot website specialist to improve our existing Jiffy Offer website, a real estate investment business serving homeowners in North Carolina’s Triangle area. This is a hands-on specialist role, not a general administrative VA position. We are improving an existing Carrot site, not rebuilding it from scratch or moving to another platform. We have a detailed website repositioning guide. We need someone who can implement it while protecting existing SEO performance, improving the seller experience, and ensuring website leads reliably reach GoHighLevel. Scope of work Initial priorities: Audit the existing website, forms, tracking, and SEO performance before making changes. Update the homepage hero, calls to action, trust elements, and mobile layout. Implement an address-first lead form with contact details and a preferred-contact-method field. Recommend whether to use native Carrot forms or an embedded GoHighLevel form based on the requirements. Launch a short form first, with the ability to test a multi-step version later. Connect form submissions to GoHighLevel, including custom-field mapping, contact preferences, landing-page information, and hidden UTM data. Build or update thank-you pages and test the complete lead handoff. Implement and validate conversion tracking. Preserve existing ranking URLs, update on-page SEO, and handle redirects where necessary. Ongoing work: Publish city-specific and seller-situation landing pages. Create focused landing pages for marketing campaigns. Improve internal linking, mobile usability, and page performance. Test headlines, forms, and trust elements. Monitor organic traffic and conversion performance. Document changes, results, and unresolved issues. Required experience At least two years of direct Investor Carrot experience; three or more years preferred. Two or three live Carrot websites you have built or managed. A clear explanation of your personal contribution to each site. Experience with Carrot’s page builder, lead forms, SEO settings, and content tools. On-page SEO experience, including protecting existing rankings during website updates. Experience connecting website forms to a CRM. GoHighLevel experience is strongly preferred; relevant Zapier integration experience is also acceptable. Familiarity with real estate investor websites, house-buying businesses, and motivated-seller funnels. Clear written English and the ability to explain technical decisions in plain language. Ability to work from a written guide, manage implementation, and flag dependencies before making consequential changes. Generic WordPress experience alone does not meet the Carrot-specific requirement. Helpful additional skills Google Analytics 4 and Google Search Console. Google Tag Manager. UTM tracking and source attribution. GoHighLevel custom fields and workflow routing. Zapier or webhook integrations. Meta Pixel and Conversions API. Conversion-rate optimization and landing-page testing. Basic HTML/CSS. Mobile accessibility and page-speed optimization. Hours and budget Hourly, part-time: approximately 10–20 hours per week to start. Target budget: $8–$12 USD per hour. Please provide your current hourly rate and weekly availability. Final selection and any exceptions to the target range require owner approval. To apply Please include: How many years you have worked specifically with Investor Carrot and approximately how many sites you have built or managed. Two or three live Carrot website URLs, with a brief explanation of what you personally built or changed on each. One measurable result from your website, SEO, or conversion work: what you changed, the relevant time period, and what happened. A brief description of your GoHighLevel or Zapier integration experience. Your current hourly rate and availability for 10–20 hours per week. Applications without live Carrot URLs will not qualify for the primary shortlist. Qualified applicants will receive a short written screening questionnaire before final interviews with the owner. Please do not request website or CRM credentials during screening. No account access will be provided at the application stage.', 1, 'HOURLY', 207000.00, 310000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a4de8020-9be2-5a89-8d67-2eca09cc0382', '93fbdb17-0a5e-51fb-a8bd-25092dae7d22', 'Code Reviewer', 'Hi Looking for a programmer who can review large pieces of code to identify how the code works, where certain key functionalities are implemented. May require travel within US (expenses paid). Should know C/C++ and Java. Thanks, Rahul Copperpod is one of the world''s leading technology research and forensics firms, with an acute focus on management and monetization of intellectual property assets. With offices in US and Asia, our global team of consultants has helped clients realize over $1 billion in revenues from patent licensing, jury verdicts and patent portfolio transactions.', 1, 'HOURLY', 775000.00, 3229000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0c9e446c-f579-51a2-b5fb-9ec5caaf136b', 'fed68a2f-5036-5915-9ee5-eedbd1db927b', 'QA Analyst for Software Testing', 'Keeping Current Matters (KCM), part of HousingWire, makes a subscription software platform that real estate agents use to create and share marketing content, at the national and local market level. We are hiring a contract QA analyst to test new features, enhancements and bug fixes before they reach our members. Additionally we are in the process of building a new product (slated to release in Q1 2027) that will require significant testing support. You will test the product the way a real estate agent or loan professional uses it: on desktop, in our iOS and Android apps, and in mobile browsers. A core part of the job is working through the typical workflows and confirming that content posts correctly from our platform to Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, and LinkedIn. This is a hands-on manual testing role. You will not write automated test code. • Hours: 15 to 25 hours per week to start, expected to grow. Additional hours may be available for testing other tools across the company, based on need. • Schedule: Flexible to be coordinated and set on a weekly basis • Location: Remote, U.S. based, Eastern or Central time zones What you will do • Run release testing. Work through a release checklist on desktop browsers, the iOS and Android apps, and mobile browsers before each launch. Give a clear go or no-go recommendation with the reasons. • Prepare for the new product launch. Test our new product as it is built ahead of its Q1 2027 release. Help create its test checklist and confirm it is ready before launch. • Verify bug fixes. Confirm each fix works, and check that it did not break anything nearby. • Test social media posting end to end. Connect accounts, create content, post or schedule it, and confirm it appears correctly on Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, and LinkedIn. • Test account connections. Check connecting, disconnecting, and reconnecting social accounts, plus what happens when a connection expires or loses permissions. • Write clear bug reports. Log issues in Linear or per team advised process with exact steps, device, operating system, browser, expected vs. actual results, and screenshots or screen recordings. • Capture technical evidence. Use browser developer tools to collect console errors and failed network requests so developers can find the cause faster. • Build and maintain test cases. Create and update the regression checklist, meaning the standard set of checks that confirm existing features still work after a change. • Flag patterns. Tell us when the same area keeps breaking, or when a platform change (for example, a new Instagram rule) affects posting. • Collaborate cross-functionally. Work closely with Member Success, Product, UI/UX and Engineering to share findings, and streamline the testing process as part of Product Releases. Required experience • 3 or more years of manual QA testing on a web-based software product • Testing native mobile apps on real iOS and Android devices, including installing test builds through TestFlight and Google Play internal testing • Testing responsive websites in mobile browsers • Writing test cases and regression checklists, not only following them • Bug reports that a developer can act on without follow-up questions • Comfort using browser developer tools to read console errors and network requests • Preferred: Hands-on experience with social media platforms (business accounts on Facebook, Instagram), TikTok, and LinkedIn • Experience with an issue tracker such as Linear, Jira, or similar • Experience working on a distributed, remote team, including communicating through Slack and working in Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Drive) • Clear written communication and the judgment to say "this is not ready to ship" when it isn''t Nice to have • QA experience with a social media scheduling or publishing tool (for example Hootsuite, Buffer, Later, or Sprout Social) • Experience testing integrations that connect to outside platforms through account login and permission screens • Familiarity with marketing or content creation software • Experience in real estate technology Not required • Coding or test automation. This role is manual testing. We may add automation later as a separate effort. • Real estate knowledge. We will teach you how agents use the product.', 1, 'HOURLY', 904000.00, 1162000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('bba13ce5-da54-5733-93db-fa50a5fcc7f6', '727bb328-44bf-5f86-bf1f-a52bc1b36d3d', 'Làm ứng dụng web thương mại điện tử lĩnh vực bất động sản', 'Mình có nhu cầu làm website sàn thương mại điện tử đăng tin bất động sản. - Giai đoạn 1 là quản trị viên tự soạn thảo và đăng tin cho người dùng, phân quyền quản trị, tính phí tin đăng theo lượt click, công cụ tìm kiếm, bộ lọc và các tùy chọn sắp xếp tin đăng, SEO tốt, tối ưu cho mobile. - Giai đoạn 2 bổ sung thêm tính năng cho phép người dùng tự đăng nhập và đăng tin giống như các sàn khác trên thị trường, đánh giá và nhận xét tin đăng, báo cáo tin đăng/người dùng, lưu hoặc duyệt các tin đăng đã xem gần đây, người đăng quản lý lead và tùy chọn CTA, admin quản lý/phê duyệt các cấp độ tài khoản người dùng. - Giai đoạn 3 bổ sung tính năng thông báo từ hệ thống, nhắn tin nội bộ, thanh toán phí dịch vụ trực tuyến.', 1, 'FIXED', 30000000.00, 100000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('1f7f7d5c-3186-5a7d-8f00-df8d6022f063', '4ab7aeeb-3114-582c-8e21-025a366d4259', 'Phát triển website quản lý nội bộ', 'PHÁT TRIỂN HỆ THỐNG QUẢN TRỊ NỘI BỘ (ERP/CRM) BẤT ĐỘNG SẢN Cần tìm Freelancer phát triển website quản lý nội bộ cho công ty BĐS. Hệ thống tập trung vào quản lý giỏ hàng, khách hàng và dòng tiền giao dịch. Các tính năng chính: Quản lý giỏ hàng: Cập nhật trạng thái sản phẩm (trống/cọc/bán) theo thời gian thực (Real-time). Quản lý CRM & Phân quyền: Phân cấp dữ liệu chặt chẽ giữa Sale - Quản lý - Admin. Tính toán tự động: Hệ thống tính hoa hồng, bảng tiến độ thanh toán và xuất file hợp đồng mẫu. Dashboard: Báo cáo doanh số và hiệu suất nhân viên trực quan.', 1, 'FIXED', 4000000.00, 13000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('9d53bc5f-b20a-548a-86ed-9474c40a25d0', '1aaef433-15b3-598d-9b7d-923ccfeff6de', 'Website PHP Thuần muốn chuyển đổi sang Laravel', 'Tôi có 1 website bất động sản, mã nguồn của website hiện đang là PHP thuần. Giờ tôi muốn chuyển đổi toàn bộ sang Laravel. Yêu cầu: - Không làm thay đổi cấu trúc link ảnh hưởng đến SEO.', 1, 'FIXED', 3000000.00, 8000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e476892a-082a-5a6f-a1cb-900d16dcc4ef', '22c24f33-95f4-574f-9848-7b2953c412da', 'Test ứng dụng quán lý nhà trọ', 'Hi. Mình cần tìm bạn chuyên test manual về ứng dụng quán lý nhà trọ (android, ios). Yêu cầu có test case rỏ ràng, có thể gửi mình khi ứng tuyển. Thời gian thì linh hoạt, không cố định. Do còn nhiều dự án nên có thể làm lâu dài', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 2000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f0f15f5e-a20c-5e62-a54a-f1abf3759c6e', '18fddddf-e3cf-5c10-a21f-222e615ea971', 'Mình đang có nhu cầu làm website cung cấp thông tin dự án bất động sản', 'Mình đang có nhu cầu làm website cung cấp thông tin dự án bất động sản tương tự trang này: https://www.pkdvinhomeshalong.com/', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 3000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b024605b-f68b-5f15-9315-1a5994b81550', '6f2cffd6-df6f-5939-b5f4-a9f3885cfffd', 'Manual QA & REST API Testing via Postman', 'We need a freelancer to perform manual QA and REST API testing for a small project. The work includes testing endpoints, validating responses, identifying issues, and documenting results clearly. This is a fixed-price task for someone who can work independently, communicate clearly, and deliver accurate testing outcomes. Please apply if you have experience with manual testing and API validation.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('62983e29-59b8-5da9-bb91-42054f1febec', '140f7dd3-58d9-5177-bc30-62dcf9404875', 'AI Browser Automation Developer – Playwright / Puppeteer / Node.js', 'Senior AI Browser Automation Developer – Playwright / Puppeteer / Node.js Project-Based Contract | Experienced Developers Only We are looking for an experienced developer to build a standalone, AI-assisted browser automation system for our digital marketing operations. The system will automate repetitive workflows across third-party websites, including business directory submissions, content publishing, and structured form submissions. We need someone with strong experience building intelligent browser automation, not just basic scripts or record-and-replay bots. What We''re Looking to Build A standalone automation engine capable of: Navigating different websites and dynamically identifying form fields Completing multi-step forms using structured input data Creating accounts and submitting approved content where supported Handling unexpected page changes and workflow interruptions Pausing for human assistance when CAPTCHA, verification, or missing information prevents progress Resuming workflows and reporting results with supporting evidence Providing an API or similar interface for future integration The system should combine reliable browser automation with AI-assisted decision-making where appropriate. Required Experience Strong Node.js/backend development experience Advanced Playwright or Puppeteer experience Experience with AI/LLM-driven browser agents Dynamic form handling and browser session management Building reliable automation with error handling and recovery API development and clean, maintainable architecture Bonus: Experience with browser automation for SEO, directories, content publishing platforms, and human-in-the-loop workflows. Important We understand that some websites restrict automation. We are not looking for CAPTCHA bypass solutions. The system should recognize unsupported actions and provide a practical human-assisted workflow. Deliverables A working standalone automation engine, source code, technical documentation, and a demonstration using agreed test workflows. The detailed project specification and target websites will be shared with shortlisted candidates. To Apply Please provide: Examples of complex browser automation systems you have personally built. Your experience using AI/LLMs with Playwright or Puppeteer. How you approach dynamic forms, session recovery, and human intervention. Your preferred technical approach for this project. Please apply only if you have hands-on experience building and deploying complex browser automation systems.', 1, 'FIXED', 1421000.00, 1421000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('6b7b2c72-b69d-5adf-b8b2-a56348dd6a80', 'b233995d-7aff-541e-bcf3-b1db2458f7e4', 'SDET Software Development Engineer in Test - Location Requirement — Strictly Mohali, India Only', 'Location Requirement — Strictly Mohali, India Only Applicants must currently reside in Mohali, Punjab, India. If you are located outside Mohali, please do not apply. Applications from candidates outside Mohali will not be considered. This requirement is mandatory, with no exceptions. We are seeking an experienced SDET to support test automation and quality assurance for a software development project. The role involves designing and implementing automated test cases, improving test coverage, identifying defects, and collaborating with development teams to ensure reliable software delivery. You should be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment and contributing to continuous improvement of testing processes. This is a full-time opportunity for someone who can help maintain high-quality standards throughout the development lifecycle.', 1, 'HOURLY', 129000.00, 181000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('7bdf0f76-7433-56d5-aca4-eacdec772e6a', 'c9f1f863-e13b-5157-8ca5-d2930df87587', 'Middle Automation Test Engineer (Java)', 'Mô tả công việc Thiết kế, xây dựng và thực thi các test case/test script cho Web Application. Phát triển và duy trì các kịch bản Automation Test bằng Java. Thực hiện Functional, Regression và UI Testing. Phát hiện, ghi nhận và theo dõi lỗi trên Jira/Redmine. Phân tích kết quả kiểm thử, đề xuất cải tiến nhằm nâng cao chất lượng sản phẩm. Phối hợp với BA, Developer và các bên liên quan để đảm bảo chất lượng phần mềm. Yêu cầu Từ 3 năm kinh nghiệm Automation Testing. Có ít nhất 3 năm kiểm thử Web. Thành thạo Java để phát triển Automation Test. Có kinh nghiệm với Playwright, Selenium hoặc công cụ Automation tương đương. Sử dụng JUnit5 hoặc framework test tương tự. Hiểu quy trình phát triển phần mềm (SDLC). Có kiến thức về JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML. Thành thạo Jira hoặc Redmine. Tiếng Anh đọc hiểu tài liệu kỹ thuật.', 1, 'FIXED', 20000000.00, 22000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('4945d84e-fe3f-50de-8071-148d0cfdf348', '2f00f7da-0dd6-57ee-872b-75a11e9f1598', 'QA Tester Needed for Automotive App — Comprehensive Pre-Launch Testing Across Mobile', '**QA Tester for Automotive App — Full Pre-Launch Testing Across Mobile, Tablet and Desktop** **Fixed budget: $1,000 USD** **Duration: 11 consecutive days, including weekends** **Daily meetings through Upwork are mandatory** We need an experienced QA tester to thoroughly test an automotive app before launch. You must test **every inch of the app**: every accessible screen, feature, button, form, setting, account type, and user journey. Identify bugs, document them clearly, verify developer fixes, and recommend improvements. The scope includes vehicle advertisements, car parts, Stories, search and filters, payments, automated emails, and social publishing integrations. **1. Complete Application Testing** Create a complete feature checklist at kickoff. Test: - Registration, email verification, login, logout, and password resets. - Private seller, trade seller, and brand/manufacturer accounts. - Profiles, dashboards, settings, permissions, and account separation. - Creating, previewing, publishing, editing, renewing, deleting, and marking advertisements as sold, wherever supported. - Image and video uploads, required fields, validation, and error messages. - Vehicle and car parts categories, attributes, and compatibility information. - Search, filters, sorting, listing details, and seller profiles. - Stories, enquiries, messaging, notifications, and contact forms within the app. - Social account connections and publishing. - Navigation, buttons, links, empty states, usability, and responsive layouts. Test successful journeys and failures, including invalid information, duplicate submissions, interrupted actions, and unauthorised access attempts. Add any newly discovered features to the checklist. **2. Automated Email Testing and Missing Email Audit** Review every user journey to identify automated emails that work, fail, contain errors, or are missing entirely. Cover: - Registration, verification, and welcome messages. - Account approval or rejection, where applicable. - Password resets and account changes. - Payment confirmations, receipts, and failed payments. - Subscriptions, renewals, cancellations, and expiry, where supported. - Advertisement publication, rejection, expiry, and renewal. - Enquiries and other relevant account activity. Verify triggers, recipients, delivery, timing, subjects, wording, branding, personalisation, buttons, links, and display across devices. **If an action should generate an email but none has been implemented, flag it so our developer can create it.** Deliver an email audit showing the action, account type, expected recipient, and status: - Working. - Incorrect. - Not delivered. - Missing and needs to be created. Recommend the purpose and key content of missing emails, then retest after implementation. **3. Payment Testing** Test payments for trade and private sellers, plus payment features available to other account types. Cover successful, failed, cancelled, and duplicate payment attempts; confirmations; receipts; and subscriptions, renewals, upgrades, cancellations, and refunds wherever supported. Verify that payments correctly update account status, permissions, and advertisement access. Use approved payment test credentials. Live charges require prior approval. **4. Create and Verify 300 Accounts** Create: - **100 trade seller accounts.** - **100 private seller accounts.** - **100 brand/manufacturer accounts.** Verify registration, account classification, permissions, automated emails, and dashboard access. Maintain an organised record of accounts and verification results. **Business Email Testing Infrastructure** Trade seller and brand/manufacturer registrations accept only custom business-domain email addresses. The tester must provide their own custom domain and email system supporting **200 distinct test addresses**: - 100 for trade seller accounts. - 100 for brand/manufacturer accounts. Mailboxes, aliases, or a catch-all setup may be used if each account has a unique accepted address and its automated emails can be received, identified, and verified. Confirm compatibility with our developer at kickoff. Maintain the setup throughout the project and retesting period. **All domain and email setup costs are included in the $1,000 budget. Do not include email addresses or other contact details in your proposal. Describe your setup without sharing contact information.** **5. Create and Verify 1,000 Advertisements** Create **1,000 test advertisements**, including vehicles and car parts, distributed across relevant account types. Agree the allocation at kickoff. Vehicle listings must cover: - Different makes and models, including multiple models from the same make. - Different years, prices, mileage, fuel types, transmissions, body types, engine sizes, colours, and locations. - Electric, hybrid, and other supported vehicle categories. Car parts listings must cover: - Different categories, brands, conditions, and prices. - Parts for different vehicle makes, models, and years. - Compatibility with multiple vehicles, where supported. - Part numbers, descriptions, images, availability, and delivery or collection options, where supported. Verify accurate saving, display, ownership, search visibility, and management permissions. Approved scripts may support bulk creation, but manual functional testing and verification of resulting records are required. **6. Search, Filters and Sorting** Test every vehicle and car parts filter individually and in combination. Verify: - Selecting a make displays the correct models. - Changing a make clears incompatible model selections. - Results match selected filters and exclude non-matching listings. - Each category displays appropriate filters. - Price, year, mileage, and other ranges handle boundaries and invalid values correctly. - Keyword searches work with makes, models, part names, and part numbers where supported. - Result counts, sorting, and pagination remain accurate. - Filters can be changed, removed, and reset. - Empty results show a clear message. - Filter selections behave correctly when opening a listing and returning to results. - Search and filters work across agreed devices and browsers. Use known test listings with recorded attributes to compare expected and actual results. **7. Stories — 500 Posts Daily for 11 Days** In addition to the advertisements, create and verify **500 story posts every day for 11 consecutive days: 5,500 stories in total**. Distribute posts across eligible account types and different accounts. Test: - Creation, uploads, previews, and publishing. - Supported formats, file sizes, and upload limits. - Viewing, playback, navigation, and display. - Visibility, permissions, ordering, and expiry. - Deletion, interactions, notifications, and other available functions. - Failed uploads, interrupted connections, duplicates, and validation errors. Approved automation may support volume, but manual functional testing and successful-post verification are required. Provide daily posting totals, account distribution, verification results, and defects. Coordinate volume testing with our developer in the approved test environment. **8. Facebook and Instagram Publishing Integration** Set up the authorised Meta business assets, Facebook Pages, and Instagram professional accounts required to test publishing for **trade seller and brand/manufacturer accounts**. After publishing an advertisement in the automotive app, test publishing it directly to the seller’s connected Facebook Page and Instagram account. Verify: - Connection, authorisation, disconnection, and reconnection. - Successful publishing through the app. - Correct images, listing details, prices, captions, and links wherever supported. - Publication to the correct seller’s social accounts. - Separation between sellers’ permissions and social assets. - Expired permissions, connection failures, publishing failures, retries, and duplicate submissions. - Clear confirmations and error messages. Agree the number of test social assets at kickoff. Separate social accounts are not automatically required for all 200 business seller accounts. Use dedicated, authorised test assets and follow the platforms’ requirements. **Social asset setup and integration testing are included in the fixed budget. These integrations are product features to be tested; project communication will remain on Upwork.** **9. Device and Browser Coverage** Test across **Apple and Android phones and tablets**, plus desktop browsers. Required coverage includes: - Representative iPhone generations and screen sizes, including standard, Plus, Pro, and Pro Max. - Representative iPad, iPad mini, iPad Air, and iPad Pro configurations. - Samsung Galaxy phones and representative devices from other Android manufacturers. - Samsung Galaxy Tab and representative Android tablets. - Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge, and Samsung Internet where applicable. Cover agreed current and older supported operating-system versions. If native apps are supplied, test both iOS and Android apps. Check portrait and landscape layouts, touch controls, scrolling, keyboards, uploads, and core journeys. Physical devices are required for core testing. Disclose any supplementary cloud-device or emulator testing. List available device models and agree the final coverage matrix before work begins. **10. Daily Meetings and Reporting** Attend **one scheduled meeting every day for all 11 consecutive days, including weekends**, with our team and developer **through Upwork**. Agree dates and times before the contract starts. Provide a daily written update through Upwork covering: - Testing completed and remaining. - New bugs and severity. - Fixes retested and results. - Account, advertisement, and story totals. - Blockers and next-day priorities. Report critical issues immediately. **11. Deliverables** - Complete feature checklist and test plan. - Device, operating-system, and browser coverage matrix. - Bug tracker with reproduction steps, expected and actual behaviour, severity, device details, screenshots or recordings, and retest status. - Automated email audit, including missing emails. - Verified records of 300 accounts and 1,000 advertisements. - Vehicle and parts test-data coverage. - Search, filter, and sorting results. - Daily evidence of 500 story posts, totalling 5,500. - Social publishing integration results. - Daily progress reports and meeting attendance. - Prioritised improvement recommendations. - Final launch-readiness report covering unresolved bugs, untested areas, and remaining risks. Our developer implements fixes. The tester verifies them and checks for regressions during the project. Use the approved test environment and approved or licensed content. Production changes, public test listings, public social posts, and live payments require prior approval. **12. Budget and Attendance Condition** The **$1,000 USD fixed budget** includes all agreed testing, device coverage, domain and email setup, account creation, advertisements, daily Stories, social integration setup, meetings, reports, and retesting during the 11-day period. **Daily attendance is a material requirement. Our proposed condition is that missing any scheduled daily meeting without prior written agreement reduces the total project payment to $500 USD.** Meetings cancelled or rescheduled by our team do not count as missed attendance. This condition must be expressly agreed in the Upwork contract before work begins and remains subject to Upwork’s payment and dispute processes. **To Apply** Provide: 1. Relevant marketplace or automotive QA experience. 2. Your available physical devices and proposed operating-system/browser coverage. 3. A sample bug report without personal or contact information. 4. Your plan for creating and verifying 300 accounts and 1,000 varied advertisements. 5. A description of your business-domain email testing setup, without including actual addresses. 6. Your approach to testing makes, models, parts compatibility, search, and combined filters. 7. Your plan for posting and verifying 500 Stories daily. 8. Relevant Facebook and Instagram integration testing experience. 9. Your approach to identifying missing automated emails. 10. Confirmation that you can attend all 11 daily meetings through Upwork. 11. Confirmation that the full agreed scope is included in **$1,000 USD**. Please keep all applications, communication, meetings, and payments on Upwork.', 1, 'FIXED', 25832000.00, 25832000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('db95a556-b400-56cb-a24a-efb6ef100a4e', 'e33b9267-e504-540a-8440-a7cc50a75b6c', 'QA Tester for Payment Systems in Australia (ANZ Users)', 'We are looking for freelance QA testers located in Australia to help us test the checkout and payment flows of various websites. In this role, you will check how local payment methods work for real users. You will be asked to: - Register an account on a website. - Deposit funds using an ANZ bank account. - Request a withdrawal of those funds. - Record your screen during the process and report your findings. Requirements: - You must currently reside in Australia. - You must have access to an ANZ bank account. - You must be able to provide clear screen recordings of your test sessions. How pay works: - You are paid for each completed test. - We provide the funds for the test separately; you will never use your own money for the deposits. - Reliable testers who provide clear and timely reports receive more assignments and can earn more over time. This job post was prepared with AI assistance and reviewed by our team.', 1, 'FIXED', 129000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('47c800fb-5527-5528-91eb-f3298ddbfce9', 'd81811b6-a82c-5c18-91d1-680d3d217f74', 'QA tester Morocco', 'I’m looking for a QA tester based in Morocco to test casino and sports betting websites on both mobile and desktop. The role involves checking website functionality, usability, links, forms, and overall user experience across different devices.', 1, 'FIXED', 129000.00, 129000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('79488eb3-bd76-5120-9a03-f12ab609b46e', 'd1bd26b8-6081-5f45-abed-606cd78d9835', 'UX QA Tester for Web App', 'We’re looking for a UX QA Tester to review our web app from both usability and functionality perspectives. This is a fixed $10 job for about 1 hour of testing. We want someone who can think like a real user, identify where people might hesitate or get confused, and catch issues that are broken or inconsistent. You’ll test core user flows as a first-time user, including onboarding, the main dashboard, and one key action such as checkout, booking, or upload. Please document usability issues, functional bugs, and inconsistent behavior across devices and browsers, rate each issue by severity, and provide clear recommendations. The final deliverable should be a structured report with screenshots or screen recordings, severity ratings, and a short list of the top 3–5 fixes to prioritize.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f8d938aa-22de-5e0a-8e7f-6087bed0e97d', '0f00854f-943b-5f21-9ba7-8d32dcc2ee54', 'Verifying website functionality through manual testing', 'Website functionality verification via manual testing The website requires manual testing. This includes verifying that navigation between pages works correctly and ensuring that all buttons on the site are clickable and functional.', 1, 'FIXED', 775000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('ad9c0f3c-ecd1-5505-be0d-3e9c2043c2f2', '5469ce43-d1f3-50ac-acbf-e41b8451eb90', 'TÌM QA TESTER (2+ NĂM KN) – REMOTE & LINH HOẠT', 'Bên mình là một software team mới, đang xây dựng network QA/Tester để đảm bảo chất lượng cho các dự án web/app và các hệ thống liên quan đến trading. Hiện chưa có dự án ngay, nhưng muốn kết nối trước với các bạn QA để có thể triển khai nhanh khi có project. Hình thức làm việc: 100% remote Thời gian linh hoạt (theo tiến độ project), hoặc giờ hành chính Làm việc theo từng project (freelance) Yêu cầu: Có ít nhất 2 năm kinh nghiệm QA / Software Testing Hiểu quy trình test (test case, bug report, regression…) Có kinh nghiệm test web hoặc mobile app Ưu tiên: Có kinh nghiệm trong lĩnh vực trading / forex Đã từng test hệ thống tài chính / realtime / data-sensitive Quy trình: Review CV / kinh nghiệm Call nhanh 15–20 phút Nếu phù hợp → add vào network QA Khi có project: Bên mình sẽ contact các bạn phù hợp Trao đổi nhanh scope và bắt đầu Có thể có check nhanh theo yêu cầu project Mong muốn: Tìm QA có thể hợp tác lâu dài, làm nhiều dự án cùng nhau. Ứng tuyển gửi: CV Mô tả kinh nghiệm test (project đã làm) Tools đã sử dụng Điểm cộng: Cẩn thận, detail-oriented Chủ động, giao tiếp rõ ràng Phản hồi nhanh Đúng giờ Nếu bạn quan tâm, gửi CV qua email: [được ẩn bởi vlance] nhé (bên mình không check comment/inbox) Cảm ơn mọi người!', 1, 'FIXED', 15000000.00, 25000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('cfbea7e1-dd5e-56c6-898d-88f68f125291', '2b49128c-e522-5840-a0f6-7cadf18e3264', 'Searching QA Tester in Czech Republic', 'Hello, we are looking for testers located in Czech Republic to assist with evaluating a website we are preparing to launch. You would manually validate: The process would be: 1. Review the test plan and instructions 2. Visit the site to execute test cases 3. Complete feedback survey 4. Record testing session, blurring personal details Requirements: - Complete within 1 day - Physically located in Czech Republic - Cannot use VPN - Testing video should only show the site, no other apps/sites - The entire session must be recorded This hands-on testing will help improve platform quality before launch. Please let me know if you have the capacity and qualifications to assist with ensuring a positive user experience. Your time and feedback would be greatly appreciated!', 1, 'FIXED', 517000.00, 517000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('b9f1e3a7-6de7-5458-b655-f8526c3abee5', '925445c1-f9ea-5c47-ac6e-7671f2a42fe3', 'Searching QA Tester in France(FR)', 'Hello, we are looking for testers located in France(FR) to assist with evaluating a website we are preparing to launch. You would manually validate: The process would be: 1. Review the test plan and instructions 2. Visit the site to execute test cases 3. Complete feedback survey 4. Record testing session, blurring personal details Requirements: - Complete within 1 day - Physically located in France(FR) - Cannot use VPN - Testing video should only show the site, no other apps/sites - The entire session must be recorded This hands-on testing will help improve platform quality before launch. Please let me know if you have the capacity and qualifications to assist with ensuring a positive user experience. Your time and feedback would be greatly appreciated!', 1, 'FIXED', 2583000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e26d7a84-4f80-57cf-920e-237c112fbeee', 'c2076610-11b4-5398-920a-ac46b59c0ee7', 'Searching QA Tester in United Kingdom (UK)', 'Hello, we are looking for testers located in United Kingdom (UK) to assist with evaluating a website we are preparing to launch. You would manually validate: The process would be: 1. Review the test plan and instructions 2. Visit the site to execute test cases 3. Complete feedback survey 4. Record testing session, blurring personal details Requirements: - Complete within 1 day - Physically located in United Kingdom (UK) - Cannot use VPN - Testing video should only show the site, no other apps/sites - The entire session must be recorded This hands-on testing will help improve platform quality before launch. Please let me know if you have the capacity and qualifications to assist with ensuring a positive user experience. Your time and feedback would be greatly appreciated!', 1, 'FIXED', 2583000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('e2156292-0143-564e-b77b-7e4c51c0e2ca', 'bfc111e0-0ed1-50c9-a078-0eb163d6261f', 'Mobile App Tester From Mexico', 'We have a mobile app for payments. We need someone that helps us testing it in Mexico, since we want to roll it out there. We will hop on a call and test different app features together to see how it works in Mexico.', 1, 'HOURLY', 207000.00, 387000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('615521f3-8d48-5245-98e6-f91ea4b58c0c', 'cd6ffa9b-43af-5c7c-bc2b-17cdaa70a542', 'Word Mobile App testers needed', 'I need 5 or 6 mobile word game app testers who can use English in the game. I want detailed documentation of errors and suggested enhancements. 10 to 20 minutes a day for 8-10 days.', 1, 'FIXED', 7750000.00, 7750000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('8dc3116c-6535-5b3f-b74a-1913db207572', 'fb660234-fead-5ecc-aaee-adca69df1f89', 'Mexico: iPhone gamer in Mexico needed – test 6 mobile games (5 min each)', 'We’re building a mobile app that improves connection quality for online games, and we need a real player in Mexico to help us test game connections from a local network. This is a short, one-time task (about 2–3 hours, mostly waiting for downloads), with a chance of paid repeat tests later. What you’ll do - Install our beta app through TestFlight. We’ll send you an invite. - Turn off any other VPN or proxy. Then run the free Speedtest by Ookla app and send us a screenshot of the result (it shows your internet provider and location). - Download these 6 games from the App Store: League of Legends: Wild Rift, Fortnite, Free Fire, Call of Duty: Mobile, PUBG Mobile, Brawl Stars. - For each game, play it through our app: - Open our app and select the game. - Once our app shows it’s ready, launch the game. - Finish any required tutorial, then join a real online match with other players. The menu, training mode or tutorial doesn’t count. - Stay in the match for at least 5 minutes, then exit. If a game locks multiplayer for new accounts, play the first online mode available and tell us which one. - For each match, send us: a screenshot of our app with the game selected a screenshot at the start and at the end of the match, with the in-game ping visible if the game shows it whether you were on Wi-Fi or mobile data any lag, freezing or disconnects you noticed Requirements - You are physically located in Mexico and use a local internet provider or mobile carrier - No VPN or proxy during the test - A recent iPhone that can run Fortnite and Call of Duty: Mobile - About 15 GB of free storage - Able to finish within 3 days of hiring Spanish or English is fine.', 1, 'FIXED', 1033000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('126a85a0-6518-5c6b-a016-f1a2bd50e4c6', '77b4a068-6f77-5b4a-af63-c8c4436c287d', 'Colombia: iPhone gamer in Colombia needed – test 6 mobile games (5 min each)', 'We’re building a mobile app that improves connection quality for online games, and we need a real player in Colombia to help us test game connections from a local network. This is a short, one-time task (about 2–3 hours, mostly waiting for downloads), with a chance of paid repeat tests later. What you’ll do - Install our beta app through TestFlight. We’ll send you an invite. - Turn off any other VPN or proxy. Then run the free Speedtest by Ookla app and send us a screenshot of the result (it shows your internet provider and location). - Download these 6 games from the App Store: League of Legends: Wild Rift, Fortnite, Free Fire, Call of Duty: Mobile, PUBG Mobile, Brawl Stars. - For each game, play it through our app: - Open our app and select the game. - Once our app shows it’s ready, launch the game. - Finish any required tutorial, then join a real online match with other players. The menu, training mode or tutorial doesn’t count. - Stay in the match for at least 5 minutes, then exit. If a game locks multiplayer for new accounts, play the first online mode available and tell us which one. - For each match, send us: a screenshot of our app with the game selected a screenshot at the start and at the end of the match, with the in-game ping visible if the game shows it whether you were on Wi-Fi or mobile data any lag, freezing or disconnects you noticed Requirements - You are physically located in Colombia and use a local internet provider or mobile carrier - No VPN or proxy during the test - A recent iPhone that can run Fortnite and Call of Duty: Mobile - About 15 GB of free storage - Able to finish within 3 days of hiring Spanish or English is fine.', 1, 'FIXED', 1033000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('5681b6b7-834d-53ad-aee5-315cdce4285e', 'a2d730de-5b9f-5220-b40a-abd8f23645f1', 'Chile: iPhone gamer in Chile needed – test 6 mobile games (5 min each)', 'We’re building a mobile app that improves connection quality for online games, and we need a real player in Mexico to help us test game connections from a local network. This is a short, one-time task (about 2–3 hours, mostly waiting for downloads), with a chance of paid repeat tests later. What you’ll do - Install our beta app through TestFlight. We’ll send you an invite. - Turn off any other VPN or proxy. Then run the free Speedtest by Ookla app and send us a screenshot of the result (it shows your internet provider and location). - Download these 6 games from the App Store: League of Legends: Wild Rift, Fortnite, Free Fire, Call of Duty: Mobile, PUBG Mobile, Brawl Stars. - For each game, play it through our app: - Open our app and select the game. - Once our app shows it’s ready, launch the game. - Finish any required tutorial, then join a real online match with other players. The menu, training mode or tutorial doesn’t count. - Stay in the match for at least 5 minutes, then exit. If a game locks multiplayer for new accounts, play the first online mode available and tell us which one. - For each match, send us: a screenshot of our app with the game selected a screenshot at the start and at the end of the match, with the in-game ping visible if the game shows it whether you were on Wi-Fi or mobile data any lag, freezing or disconnects you noticed Requirements - You are physically located in Chile and use a local internet provider or mobile carrier - No VPN or proxy during the test - A recent iPhone that can run Fortnite and Call of Duty: Mobile - About 15 GB of free storage - Able to finish within 3 days of hiring Spanish or English is fine.', 1, 'FIXED', 1292000.00, 1292000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('87ecbaed-9fd2-58e5-8e1f-6866b4363056', 'bad5f768-e571-5344-926f-600d574444c8', 'Need a game developer Monthly salary 150$', 'Educational Game Developer Needed – 3D Modeling, Publishing & Bug Fixing We are looking for an experienced Game Developer who can independently manage game development from start to publishing, along with maintaining and fixing bugs in our existing and upcoming games. Responsibilities: - Develop, test, and optimize games from start to finish. - Create, modify, and integrate 3D models and game assets. - Identify and fix bugs in already-published games and games under development. - Handle game builds, testing, and publishing to the Google Play Store and other relevant platforms. - Maintain published games through regular updates, performance improvements, and bug fixes. - Ensure smooth gameplay and compatibility across different devices. Requirements: - Strong practical experience in game development. - Proficiency in Unity or Unreal Engine. - Experience with 3D modeling and asset integration. - Proven experience publishing games to the Google Play Store or other platforms. - Strong debugging, troubleshooting, and optimization skills. - Ability to work independently and take ownership of assigned projects. To Apply: Please share your portfolio, links to games you have developed or published, the game engines and 3D modeling tools you use, and examples of bugs you have fixed in previous projects. We are looking for a reliable developer interested in long-term collaboration for both existing and upcoming games.', 1, 'FIXED', 3875000.00, 3875000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f529b741-5f08-583c-b1bb-e78eb5575e34', 'eadd5b84-b23a-5250-aa76-753ed0428acc', 'Senior C++ Game Engine Developer – Legacy MMORPG Port to Android & iOS', 'Project Type: Existing MMORPG Cross-Platform Porting Original Platform: Windows PC Target Platforms: Android and iOS (Both Required) Existing Technology: Legacy C++, Windows APIs, DirectX, Visual Studio 2010-era source code Game Type: 3D Online Multiplayer RPG (MMORPG) Project Scope: Technical Assessment, Development, Optimization, Integration, Testing, and Mobile Deployment Existing Source Code Size: Approximately 15 GB PROJECT OVERVIEW We are looking for a highly experienced Senior C++ Game Developer / Game Engine Engineer or a development team specializing in porting legacy Windows PC games to modern mobile platforms. We own an existing, operational 3D MMORPG developed using an older C++ game engine originally designed for Windows. Our objective is to create fully functional versions of the existing game for both Android and iOS, allowing players to access the same game world through mobile devices. This is an existing game with its own client, server architecture, game assets, networking protocols, account database, and gameplay systems. We are not looking to recreate the entire MMORPG using a new engine unless a technical assessment determines that this is necessary. Our preference is to preserve the original architecture, gameplay mechanics, assets, and existing server infrastructure while making the necessary platform-specific modifications. Both Android and iOS must be supported. An Android-only port or an Android emulator solution will not fulfill the project requirements. EXISTING TECHNICAL ENVIRONMENT The existing game includes: Legacy Windows-based C++ game client. DirectX-based 3D rendering architecture. Visual Studio 2010-era project structure. Windows-specific libraries, APIs, and dependencies. Existing MMORPG login and game server infrastructure. Microsoft SQL Server-based game databases. Real-time multiplayer networking. Character creation, movement, combat, skills, equipment, inventory, NPC interactions, and quests. Existing 3D character models, animations, textures, maps, effects, sounds, and user interface assets. Guild systems, party systems, PvP, and scheduled multiplayer war events. The game currently runs on Windows. We need a developer capable of inspecting the existing engine and identifying precisely which modules can be reused, refactored, replaced, or rebuilt for Android and iOS. ANDROID DELIVERABLES: Functional Android client. Installable development and testing APK. Release-ready Android App Bundle (AAB), where applicable. Android build project and complete source code. Documentation of dependencies, build requirements, and modifications. IOS DELIVERABLES: Functional iOS game client. Complete Xcode project. Testable iOS development builds. TestFlight-compatible build where applicable. Deployment and signing instructions. Complete updated source code and documentation. Mandatory Project Timeline and Delivery Requirements November 27, 2026: Complete development of both mobile clients and deliver fully playable, test-ready builds. November 28–30, 2026: Closed Alpha Testing with selected players (3 days). December 1–7, 2026: Public Beta Testing (7 days). December 8–11, 2026: Final bug fixes, optimization, and release preparation. December 12, 2026: Official Android and iOS Release.', 1, 'FIXED', 20666000.00, 20666000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('65a57323-5a0c-5e9e-89a4-cc72bfe6ba1d', '8ea2bfeb-4823-530e-a129-b2ce1c4cf96e', 'Product tester needed', 'We’re looking for people who are interested in trying out our product and sharing honest feedback about their experience. What you’ll do: 1. Try the assigned product(s) according to the provided instructions. 2. Share honest, detailed feedback about your experience. 3. Complete a short review covering the product’s quality, usability, and overall impressions. Provide suggestions for improvement, if any. Who we’re looking for: 1. People interested in trying new products. 2. Individuals who can provide thoughtful, genuine feedback. 3. Reliable testers who can complete the task within the agreed timeframe. If you do well we will give you 5 stars for your Upwork profile. We also have multiple products to test so we can hire you multiple times.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('ede8b659-652d-582e-a224-5fbad60f5dfd', '27bb8ede-049e-586b-b773-b321a9547b64', 'Senior Website QA Engineer', 'We are seeking an experienced QA engineer to conduct a comprehensive quality and functionality audit of our travel booking website. The work includes testing pages, features, forms, navigation, desktop and mobile responsiveness, and RTL/English/Hebrew interfaces. You will identify UI/UX issues, broken links, functional bugs, and performance concerns, while reviewing search, filtering, account flows, and booking-related interfaces. Testing must be non-destructive, with no live bookings, payments, cancellations, or production data changes. Please deliver a structured bug report with screenshots, reproduction steps, severity levels, and practical improvement recommendations. Share examples of similar QA projects, your testing tools, timeline, and project price.', 1, 'HOURLY', 258000.00, 517000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('0055a414-099d-54b2-800e-2336e48dbc66', '9510d217-035c-5c3b-867b-afc512d608b9', 'Bubble App Developer for Complex App', 'Not a rideshare app, but similar backend complexity We’re looking for an experienced developer to help build, test, polish, and deploy a complex app similar to Uber or Lyft. The project includes creating a smooth user experience, refining workflows, and ensuring the app is ready for launch. You should be comfortable working on a detailed product and helping improve performance, usability, and overall quality before deployment. App and backend errors cleared …', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('48478eaf-1d71-5924-9fb5-b44f4f2e0e72', 'ef5c8a5f-c122-55b4-aa1f-f7fc83483c8b', 'Belgium - Orange - Mobile Testing', 'Looking for freelancers in Belgium with Orange simcard and data connection to test our subscription based services.', 1, 'HOURLY', 155000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('bfdf80ea-acf2-541a-ae6c-f389ef918b44', '88d35cf3-1f7a-5fd1-82f3-0c80b0ccf8a8', 'Looking for Assistance on Testing of VAS Services', 'Looking for assitance to test our Web/Mobile App digital services on Telecom operator network like Etisalat to check end to end flow of the services.', 1, 'FIXED', 258000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('cd1ec6a5-620f-54d7-8d58-d085e1f20a09', 'bc7d212a-dc11-59d7-a24e-0783b8b41f59', 'Competitors Retention Checking | Brazil, LATAM', 'We are looking for testers to check the work of retention communication (email and push-up notifications) across 6 platforms during a month. The tester must have access to at least one of the following: - 1 email address that has never been used before for a project with our company - An Android smartphone that supports the latest version of the apps - A PC or laptop for filling our report The tester will need to: - Check several accounts daily - Make a screen recording of every notification received - Report any errors, broken links, or unexpected results Testers must be available throughout the f1 month period and able to provide clear screen recordings from their device.', 1, 'FIXED', 2325000.00, 2325000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('1c54640b-2dea-517b-bbdc-1c4b265bb3bb', 'a25a3637-186a-5b6f-ba63-ed0debc197e6', 'Build responsive WP website on supplied test server', 'WordPress developer needed to build out 18-20 page website for an existing company using Salient theme and WPBakery Page Builder. Temporary access to our test server will be provided, along with the project scope, page content, site structure and design/layout outline. The primary work is translating those plans into properly built, responsive pages—no direct brand design or content writing. Work includes: Creating pages with provided optimized page names and URLs. Creating menus from these pages and placing internal links. Building page layouts with the specified rows, columns, content sections, buttons and image placements. Applying consistent typography, spacing, colors and styling throughout. Modify theme appearance to brand update as provided. Creating desktop, tablet, and mobile menus, dropdowns and internal links. Setting up required functions, such as contact forms, galleries, sliders, hero images and videos as specified. Adjusting layouts for desktop, tablet and mobile. Testing links, menus, forms and responsive behavior. Keeping pages organized and easy for company to edit and update after contract is completed. Some visual and written content will be added by company brand manager afterward, including background images, photographs and finishing details. Clearly identified placeholders are acceptable in those locations, but the underlying layouts and functionality should be complete and ready for those additions. Optional additional work: Optimizing existing portfolio images, including conversion to WebP and/or AVIF where supported and updating file image names for local optimization. Please indicate whether you offer this and price it separately if needed. Experience with WPBakery is strongly preferred. Experience with Salient theme a plus. Please share relevant examples you have personally built and describe your experience implementing supplied layouts and content. All work will take place in the provided hosting environment. Publishing or changing the live website is outside this initial scope. The company will add finishing touches and launch the redesign themselves when all details are in place. Detailed scope and development outlines will be provided.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('a2756fe9-e891-5ee2-a5b5-1d933a2df5b6', '2e471b19-dc5f-5538-a8dd-b3fb52a40c9b', 'Mobile App Development Project', 'We’re looking for a developer to help build a mobile app for a small business. The project includes creating a user-friendly interface, implementing core app features, and supporting testing and launch preparation. You should be comfortable working independently, communicating clearly, and delivering reliable work on schedule. If you have experience building practical mobile apps and can help turn ideas into a polished product, we’d like to hear from you.', 1, 'HOURLY', 258000.00, 517000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('8e45c878-9e80-52d9-b39d-49a3526f9306', '5f73c81a-43b8-5a59-8005-1d61c1623fad', 'Interactive Vertical Touch Screen App Developer', 'We need a developer to build an interactive app for a vertical touch screen. The project includes creating a user-friendly interface, implementing smooth navigation, and ensuring the app works well on a vertical display. You will also help with testing and refining the experience for a polished final product. Please share relevant examples of similar projects and your approach to designing for vertical touch screen use.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('f147e6d5-b309-5fac-9f66-35074b39f225', '5b0a2e1b-0e36-54dc-836d-80b34e2227bc', 'Hỗ trợ TikTok API for Developers', 'Tôi cần 1 người có thể xin được TikTok API for Developers. - Tư vấn quy trình đăng ký TikTok API for Developers cho ứng dụng/doanh nghiệp - Hỗ trợ chuẩn bị hồ sơ, thông tin kỹ thuật theo yêu cầu của TikTok (App info, use case, scope API…) - Hướng dẫn hoặc trực tiếp hỗ trợ submit application trên TikTok for Developers Portal - Tư vấn lựa chọn các API phù hợp - Hỗ trợ test kết nối API Mục tiêu là đăng ký & sử dụng API đúng quy định của TikTok.', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 5000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('ead5d058-c08c-5988-8ce6-3cf0365df0fa', 'a4b0f7b3-64f2-52fd-8402-be6f4e0a4a41', 'Cần một bạn kiểm thử tính năng cho app đang chạy', 'Cần một bạn kiểm thử tính năng cho app đang chạy cho thuê xe. - Kiểm tra tính ổn định của các chức năng chính trong quá trình sử dụng - Ghi nhận và báo lại các lỗi hoặc vấn đề phát sinh (nếu có) trong quá trình trải nghiệm'' - Ưu tiên ứng viên đã từng tham gia kiểm thử ứng dụng (App testing / QA testing) hoặc có kinh nghiệm sử dụng nhiều ứng dụng di động', 1, 'FIXED', 300000.00, 500000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00');

