    updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at; you are building a cinematic, frictionless conversion funnel. The site must look and feel like a high-end streaming service (e.g., Netflix, Hulu, HBO Max). * Theme: 1920s Art Deco. * Color Palette: Strict premium gold-on-black. * Vibe: Wealthy, historical, sleek, and highly professional. Standard, bright, "template-looking" creator sites will be rejected immediately. Scope of Work & Deliverables: This is a one-time, fixed-price backend build. All video files, logos, and copy are completed and will be provided via cloud storage. Your deliverables include: * Custom Domain Integration: Seamlessly connect our custom domain (princeofblackwallstreet.com) to the Podia platform with all SSL and security protocols active. * Premium Landing Page Design: Design a single, mobile-optimized sales page completely free of distracting menus. The sole focus is driving visitors to watch the embedded series trailer and click the "Unlock Vault" call-to-action button. * Private Video Vault Setup: Upload, correctly title, and structure 51 gated video episodes (Episodes 11–61) into a premium "Private Vault." The layout must be highly intuitive and binge-friendly for mobile users. * Payment Gateway Integration: Connect Stripe and PayPal, setting the digital "Vault Pass" product to a strict one-time fee of $20.00. Ensure zero friction on the checkout page. * Automated Email Capture & Tagging: Configure Podia’s native email marketing backend so every buyer is automatically captured, permanently tagged as "Series Buyer" for our upcoming book launch, and sent a customized, automated welcome receipt. * Speed & Stress Optimization: Compress all thumbnail assets and optimize page architecture so the site does not freeze, crash, or abandon sales when hit with sudden viral traffic surges from TikTok and Instagram. Required Milestones & Quality Checks: To ensure technical perfection before our hard launch, you will be required to perform a "$1 Stress Test." You will temporarily set the Vault Pass price to $1.00 so our team can execute a live transaction to verify that the payment clears, the vault unlocks instantly, and the email is correctly tagged in the audience dashboard. Ideal Freelancer Profile: * Expertise: Landing Page Design, UI/UX, Sales Funnels, E-commerce Setup, and Podia. * Hours: This is a fixed-price project ($300). We expect this to take an expert roughly 10 to 15 hours total. * Delivery: The fully tested site must be handed over within 7 to 14 days of the contract start date. To Apply, You Must Answer These Screening Questions: * Please provide direct links to previous Podia sites (or similar landing pages) you have built that feature a dark, premium, cinematic, or Art Deco aesthetic. (Applications with only bright/generic templates will be declined). * How will you ensure the mobile load speed remains under 2.5 seconds to prevent traffic bounce from social media apps? * Have you successfully set up automated customer tagging and email sequences within Podia''s native ecosystem before? * Do you agree to the final $1 live transaction stress-test before the final milestone is released?', 1, 'FIXED', 7750000.00, 7750000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('c667d6d3-56a7-5ee9-8cda-51bb513bf199', 'dbfdc9f6-5a3a-532f-bff4-93daac6740ac', 'Kotlin / Android TV SDK Engineer: Embed Interactive Video in Partner TV Apps', 'Adventr is a US AI entertainment company. Our platform powers interactive, branching video experiences (games, shows, personalized content) across web, mobile and TV. We need a hands-on Kotlin engineer to build a reusable Android SDK that lets partners embed our existing experiences inside their Android TV, Google TV and Fire TV apps. This is not a native rewrite: you''ll evaluate our existing web player and reuse it where possible, including a WebView and JavaScript bridge if that''s the right call. You should have: • 4+ years of Android, with strong production Kotlin • Shipped TV apps (please link them) and a solid grasp of D-pad focus and remote input • Experience building libraries or SDKs that other apps consume (AAR, Gradle, versioning) • Media3/ExoPlayer and WebView/hybrid experience is a big plus Deliverables: 1. A versioned AAR with a documented API that a developer can integrate into a fresh TV project in under an hour 2. A sample app that plays an Adventr experience end to end, fully operable by remote 3. Auth and analytics events working against our APIs 4. Testing on Google TV, Fire TV and the emulator, plus integration docs Remote and worldwide, with at least 3 hours of overlap with US Eastern Time. We''re looking for someone who flags unknowns early and ships in weeks, not months.', 1, 'HOURLY', 517000.00, 1162000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('69a8ee13-4d19-5a70-9d32-2900d8ff4bf1', '2f908d83-6abe-50d8-80cb-fb952fbdcf84', 'macOS Video Editor Tester — Final Cut Pro, Premiere Pro or DaVinci Resolve Experience', 'We’re looking for an experienced Mac video editor or QA tester to test Montage Pro, a video editing app for macOS. App: https://www.rainbowfactory.uk/montage-pro/ You must have hands-on experience with comparable desktop video editing apps, such as Final Cut Pro, Adobe Premiere Pro or DaVinci Resolve. You should understand editing workflows well enough to identify broken behaviour, confusing controls and problems with the finished export. REQUIREMENTS • An Apple silicon Mac running macOS 14 or later. • Relevant experience using or testing video editing applications on macOS. • Ability to report bugs clearly, with reproducible steps and screen recordings. • Access to footage and audio you have permission to use for testing. WHAT YOU’LL TEST Create real projects and test the workflow from importing footage through to exporting the finished video. Coverage should include: • Timeline editing, multiple tracks, trimming, transitions and undo/redo. • Saving, closing and reopening projects. • Cutting clips to music beats and stabilising footage. • Titles, motion effects, colour adjustments and audio mixing. • Automatic subtitles and SRT/WebVTT export. • H.264, HEVC and ProRes exports, checking picture quality, audio sync and playback. • Performance, crashes and unexpected behaviour during normal editing. Experience with OpenFX plug-ins, Audio Units, HDR or log footage is a bonus. DELIVERABLES • A test summary showing the workflows covered and your Mac specifications. • A prioritised bug report with steps to reproduce, expected versus actual results, and screenshots or recordings. • Project files and sample exports needed to reproduce issues. • Practical usability feedback grounded in your experience with other video editors. • Retesting of reported issues after fixes. Fixed-price budget: $200. Please apply only if you have relevant macOS video editing experience. General website or mobile app testing experience alone is insufficient.', 1, 'FIXED', 5166000.00, 5166000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('c94e6668-420e-5f10-aa49-2bdf3a37a30a', '7174f810-c61f-50c0-8ac9-d7a80c8a28dc', 'Fix và tối ưu scr python liên quan đến tự động phát hiện video mới', 'Fix và tối ưu scr python liên quan đến tự động phát hiện video mới. Hiện tại, script vẫn hoạt động nhưng còn tồn tại một số vấn đề về hiệu năng, độ ổn định và khả năng mở rộng. - Rà soát lại toàn bộ logic của script Python hiện có - Fix các lỗi phát sinh trong quá trình chạy (nếu có) Ưu tiên ứng viên: - Từng làm các bài toán theo dõi nội dung mới / cập nhật dữ liệu theo thời gian - Có khả năng đề xuất phương án tối ưu tốt hơn so với logic hiện tại', 1, 'FIXED', 1000000.00, 5000000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('6b46b62e-1f02-51a1-a3ab-23f2dd6e0ecc', 'a0b2d786-6db2-5203-99e7-bed97ee7acd9', 'New differentiated website for national B2B client', 'This is new website, ground up using new brand identity, video and images, updated copy and a contact form to start. We are a very experienced cross functional branding team with top strategy, brand design and content talent. The client is a $1.5b company with 30 independent operating brands. This website is for one of those companies, a fast growing with sophisticated team of 30. We are closely connected to the client, making decisions easier to manage. We need a flexible, collaborative website professional to bring the vision for this new high-power brand to life starting Q1 2027.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1937000.00, 2583000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('d014a5e4-5904-571c-a503-71fedfa28327', '1998c8c7-4da9-5f2e-a96d-0b2d19b79da6', 'Build Sharf Website', 'We need a developer to build a Sharf-style website where users can upload, share, and discover short-form videos. The site should support video uploads, a clean user interface, and a simple way to browse and interact with content. We’re looking for someone who can create a functional prototype and help shape the initial product experience. If you have experience building video-based platforms or social media-style websites, we’d love to hear how you would approach this project.', 1, 'HOURLY', 387000.00, 775000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('990f4d51-5a31-5a22-9a05-47b2e13d7d29', '08c1ffce-fd5e-5d1e-878f-70a4e8b97ca8', 'QA Engineer for a Website Speed & Network Diagnostics Platform', 'We’re about to launch a rebuilt web platform that runs website and network tests from real test agents in several geographic locations. The tools cover: real-browser page speed (waterfall, Core Web Vitals, Lighthouse); web server timing (DNS, connect, TLS, first byte); ping, traceroute and DNS trace; email server (SMTP/IMAP/POP3) and FTP/FTPS; streaming media (HLS/DASH), DNS blacklists and regional accessibility checks. We need a QA engineer who understands what these tests measure, not just whether pages render. You’ll verify that results are correct against reference tools (WebPageTest, PageSpeed Insights, dig, curl, openssl, MXToolbox) and probe edge cases such as redirects, bad TLS certificates, timeouts and unreachable hosts. You’ll also test status and error handling across locations, account and credit limits, Stripe billing in test mode, and security behavior (internal targets must be rejected, secrets must be masked). Deliverables: a short test plan, clear bug reports with steps and evidence, and a summary per testing round. Requirements: solid web QA experience plus real networking knowledge (DNS, HTTP/2, TLS, ICMP, SMTP/FTP) and web performance (Core Web Vitals, Lighthouse, waterfalls), and comfort with command-line tools.', 1, 'HOURLY', 129000.00, 258000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('67ca8acb-b679-5c01-aedc-7a9739402ef8', '629e83e0-96a5-5930-9745-9cb0b3dcc572', 'Web Developer / 3-5 Yrs of Exp / New Freelancer Welcome', 'We’re looking for a Web Developer with 3-5 years of professional experience. Experience using AI-powered development tools is preferred. You must have C1 or C2-level English proficiency, as you’ll be working closely with US-based team members and communicating regularly with the team. How to Apply Please submit a 2-3 minute Loom video introducing yourself and briefly demonstrating your web development experience and technical skills. Applications without a Loom video will not be considered. We’ll review all applications within 2-3 days, so there’s no need to rush. Please make sure your application includes everything requested above before submitting. Thank you, and we look forward to hearing from you!', 1, 'HOURLY', 646000.00, 1033000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00'),
    ('9448f7cb-796f-570f-abe7-ef24b7daddeb', '836ae0bb-5861-5285-8135-4cad35381f5d', 'Business Analyst, Media Data & MarTech', 'We’re Part and Sum, a collective of curious people who help our clients bring new ideas to market and use data to grow businesses. Our media agency work is designed to help us learn faster, test smarter, and drive continuous improvement across channels and platforms. We’re looking for a Business Analyst to support and maintain our media data warehouse and dashboarding infrastructure. You’ll keep the dashboards in our custom-built reporting platform accurate and reliable, and you’ll be the team’s dedicated go-to for reporting needs. You’ll work closely with our Senior Measurement Scientist, who leads data strategy across our larger workstreams. You’ll provide the hands-on data, reporting, and technical support that turns that strategy into working solutions. This role suits someone who is detail-oriented and service-minded, likes keeping systems running well, and enjoys helping colleagues get answers from their data. What you’ll do Maintain and update dashboards in our custom reporting platform so they stay accurate, reliable, and easy to use. Monitor media data pipelines with the Senior Measurement Scientist, then find, diagnose, and fix data quality issues. Keep metric definitions, naming conventions, and documentation consistent across clients and reports. Work with stakeholders to scope and add new data sources, metrics, and dashboard features as needs change. Act as the team’s main point of contact for reporting requests: triage, prioritize, and deliver. Handle ad hoc analysis requests by turning business questions into clear, useful insights and recommendations. Support the MarTech stack, including tracking and tagging, platform integrations, and audience and campaign data flows, so marketing data is captured correctly and flows into reporting. QA tracking implementations and campaign data before and after launch. Explain technical work in plain language to both technical and non-technical colleagues. Who you are Must haves 2–4 years of experience in business analysis, marketing or media analytics, or a similar data role. Strong working knowledge of SQL, including writing, debugging, and optimizing queries against a data warehouse. Hands-on experience building and maintaining dashboards in a BI tool such as Looker, Looker Studio, or Tableau. Familiarity with paid media and analytics platforms such as GA4, Meta Ads, Google Ads, DV360, and Adverity, and their data structures. Working knowledge of web tracking and tagging, such as Google Tag Manager, pixels, UTMs, and event setup. Experience with cloud data warehouses such as BigQuery or Snowflake. A detail-oriented, methodical approach to data QA and troubleshooting. Service-minded and organized: comfortable managing a queue of requests from multiple stakeholders. Clear communicator who can document processes and explain findings to non-technical audiences. Nice to have Python for data cleaning, automation, or analysis. Experience with CDPs and integration tools such as Segment, Branch, or Salesforce, or with audience and campaign data flows. Exposure to dbt or other data transformation and modeling tools. Familiarity with server-side tracking, consent management, or privacy-aware measurement. Exposure to experimentation or measurement concepts such as A/B testing, incrementality, or MMM. Agency or consulting experience supporting multiple clients and workstreams.', 1, 'HOURLY', 1292000.00, 1937000.00, 'RECRUITING', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00', '2026-10-27 00:00:00+00');

